1
00:00:00,353 --> 00:00:01,953
- Wonder Dogs!
- Wonder Dogs!

2
00:00:03,685 --> 00:00:05,320
- Wonder Dogs!
- Wonder Dogs!

3
00:00:05,321 --> 00:00:06,829
(Underdog)

4
00:00:06,830 --> 00:00:08,572
(A team expected to lose)

5
00:00:08,572 --> 00:00:11,086
(rather than win)

6
00:00:11,086 --> 00:00:12,953
- Wonder Dogs!
- Wonder Dogs!

7
00:00:14,686 --> 00:00:16,419
- Wonder Dogs!
- Wonder Dogs!

8
00:00:16,420 --> 00:00:18,278
Let's give it up for them!

9
00:00:20,319 --> 00:00:22,419
Today's fifth matchup!

10
00:00:22,419 --> 00:00:24,619
This is nail-biting!

11
00:00:24,619 --> 00:00:25,653
I'm losing my mind!

12
00:00:26,486 --> 00:00:29,186
Defense, wake up! Come on!

13
00:00:31,553 --> 00:00:33,453
Who's got the back line?

14
00:00:33,453 --> 00:00:34,253
C-quick!

15
00:00:34,653 --> 00:00:36,553
Let's go! Shrug it off! Keep pushing!

16
00:00:40,219 --> 00:00:41,886
This single point is crucial.

17
00:00:41,886 --> 00:00:45,219
One more!

18
00:00:45,819 --> 00:00:47,951
This is tough.
I shouldn't have promised a Season Two.

19
00:00:47,952 --> 00:00:49,186
I'm already regretting it.

20
00:00:50,753 --> 00:00:52,153
(Crying)

21
00:00:52,153 --> 00:00:53,819
Looking back on my volleyball career...

22
00:00:53,819 --> 00:00:56,953
(Kim Yeon Koung retired
on October 15, 2025)

23
00:00:57,086 --> 00:00:59,786
Now, I want to take it easy
for the rest of my life...

24
00:01:01,753 --> 00:01:03,286
Since Kim Yeon Koung retired,

25
00:01:03,286 --> 00:01:06,219
the women's national volleyball team
has struggled.

26
00:01:06,453 --> 00:01:07,135
Right...

27
00:01:07,136 --> 00:01:08,152
(Woe is me!)

28
00:01:08,153 --> 00:01:10,186
Moving forward, I think we all need to...

29
00:01:10,186 --> 00:01:12,886
take a hard look at how
we nurture and develop younger talent...

30
00:01:12,886 --> 00:01:13,953
for the future...

31
00:01:13,954 --> 00:01:15,632
of Korean volleyball.

32
00:01:15,633 --> 00:01:18,053
(Reflections on advancing
Korean volleyball)

33
00:01:18,053 --> 00:01:20,085
Ultimately, my goal is...

34
00:01:20,086 --> 00:01:21,419
to launch an eighth pro franchise.

35
00:01:21,819 --> 00:01:24,019
Pilseung Wonder Dogs!

36
00:01:24,019 --> 00:01:25,719
(That was the birth
of the first Wonder Dogs)

37
00:01:26,219 --> 00:01:28,319
(14 underdogs)

38
00:01:28,953 --> 00:01:31,019
(including waived players,)

39
00:01:31,886 --> 00:01:34,586
(retirees, and free agents)

40
00:01:34,753 --> 00:01:35,653
Enkhsoyol!

41
00:01:35,953 --> 00:01:37,186
Where are you aiming?

42
00:01:37,753 --> 00:01:39,353
Hye In, you should be better!

43
00:01:39,586 --> 00:01:41,486
Even grinding out
a single win feels impossible.

44
00:01:42,653 --> 00:01:45,886
(The Volleyball Empress's mission
to reshape the underdogs)

45
00:01:46,753 --> 00:01:48,186
(The underdogs start breaking out...)

46
00:01:51,553 --> 00:01:53,853
(of their shells to unleash
their potential.)

47
00:01:54,019 --> 00:01:55,753
- Enkhsoyol!
- What a spike!

48
00:01:56,841 --> 00:01:58,841
(The underdog revolt)

49
00:01:59,774 --> 00:02:01,074
Unbelievable!

50
00:02:01,074 --> 00:02:03,874
The Wonder Dogs stay alive!

51
00:02:05,241 --> 00:02:06,674
(But...)

52
00:02:07,407 --> 00:02:09,674
I don't think this is just
about wins and losses.

53
00:02:10,141 --> 00:02:11,841
Since our real target is...

54
00:02:11,841 --> 00:02:15,707
founding an eighth professional club,

55
00:02:15,974 --> 00:02:20,274
we're taking every bit of this
far more seriously...

56
00:02:22,241 --> 00:02:23,441
Who else is going to step up and do it?

57
00:02:24,841 --> 00:02:25,774
You can't give up now!

58
00:02:26,774 --> 00:02:28,241
If you want to move up,
you have to evolve.

59
00:02:29,741 --> 00:02:31,774
(Keep pushing forward...)

60
00:02:31,774 --> 00:02:33,441
(toward an eighth team.)

61
00:02:33,448 --> 00:02:35,548
Head coach of the Pilseung Wonder Dogs!

62
00:02:35,549 --> 00:02:38,037
Kim Yeon Koung!

63
00:02:38,574 --> 00:02:40,707
I want to build that eighth team.

64
00:02:41,074 --> 00:02:43,074
People might brush it off
as "just a TV show."

65
00:02:43,074 --> 00:02:45,607
One more tip.

66
00:02:46,141 --> 00:02:47,641
I said one more tip!

67
00:02:47,641 --> 00:02:50,307
I've been so dialed in that I forget
cameras are even rolling.

68
00:02:50,574 --> 00:02:53,041
This show has brought out
the rawest version of me.

69
00:02:54,907 --> 00:02:56,874
(The mission to build team number eight)

70
00:02:56,874 --> 00:02:58,007
(A relentless push
to found an eighth club)

71
00:02:58,374 --> 00:02:59,774
My obsession as a head coach.

72
00:02:59,774 --> 00:03:01,174
It's wearing me out.

73
00:03:02,094 --> 00:03:03,041
(Resign, or...)

74
00:03:03,041 --> 00:03:05,041
I keep a resignation letter
in my bag at all times, so...

75
00:03:05,041 --> 00:03:06,307
Make it count!

76
00:03:06,307 --> 00:03:07,507
There are no second chances!

77
00:03:08,007 --> 00:03:10,807
(launch an eighth team.)

78
00:03:10,807 --> 00:03:12,407
The Wonder Dogs are waking up.

79
00:03:13,541 --> 00:03:15,941
(Yeon Koung's dream,)

80
00:03:16,174 --> 00:03:18,174
(reaching beyond wonder)

81
00:03:20,407 --> 00:03:24,674
(Resignation Letter)

82
00:03:26,049 --> 00:03:27,949
(Episode 1: Veteran Coach Kim Yeon Koung)

83
00:03:27,974 --> 00:03:29,541
Give me a raise.

84
00:03:29,541 --> 00:03:30,507
They're running me ragged.

85
00:03:31,774 --> 00:03:33,907
Hey there.

86
00:03:35,241 --> 00:03:38,174
This is actually the spot
where we first met.

87
00:03:38,507 --> 00:03:41,174
We went through hell back then.

88
00:03:41,441 --> 00:03:43,807
We were grinding from dawn till midnight.

89
00:03:43,807 --> 00:03:45,474
With the blood and sweat
we poured into this,

90
00:03:45,474 --> 00:03:47,241
there was no way it wasn't going to hit.

91
00:03:48,041 --> 00:03:50,541
And honestly,
if it had bombed after all that,

92
00:03:50,541 --> 00:03:53,474
you probably should've rethought...

93
00:03:53,474 --> 00:03:55,374
your entire career as a producer.

94
00:03:55,841 --> 00:03:57,041
(No life outside work,)

95
00:03:57,041 --> 00:03:58,974
(no sleep)

96
00:04:00,466 --> 00:04:04,000
(Last summer,
when volleyball consumed everything)

97
00:04:04,741 --> 00:04:07,907
That's how invested everyone was.

98
00:04:07,907 --> 00:04:08,674
Spot on.

99
00:04:08,674 --> 00:04:12,641
Especially since we drove tangible change
in the volleyball scene.

100
00:04:12,641 --> 00:04:16,741
We sent four of our roster to pro clubs.

101
00:04:17,507 --> 00:04:18,874
Starting with Lee Na Yeon.

102
00:04:18,875 --> 00:04:20,536
(Lee Na Yeon,
currently in the Pink Spiders)

103
00:04:21,041 --> 00:04:22,341
- Pyo Seung Ju.
- Seung Ju, right.

104
00:04:22,342 --> 00:04:23,978
(Pyo Seung Ju,
currently in the Pink Spiders)

105
00:04:24,841 --> 00:04:27,407
Koo Sol, who recently signed
with Hyundai Hillstate.

106
00:04:29,693 --> 00:04:31,819
- Enkhsoyol.
- Yes, Enkhsoyol.

107
00:04:31,820 --> 00:04:33,247
(Enkhsoyol had signed with Red Sparks)

108
00:04:34,041 --> 00:04:36,074
Four out of our 14 secured pro contracts.

109
00:04:36,074 --> 00:04:38,907
I know. That was the dream all along,

110
00:04:38,907 --> 00:04:41,341
so that alone made
every bit of it worth it.

111
00:04:41,341 --> 00:04:44,207
Plus, interest in women's volleyball
surged across the board.

112
00:04:44,441 --> 00:04:45,674
That was incredible to witness.

113
00:04:48,074 --> 00:04:50,074
Everything seemed...

114
00:04:50,574 --> 00:04:51,641
to be rolling smoothly,

115
00:04:54,341 --> 00:04:56,874
until you dropped that note
in my hand during the finale.

116
00:04:57,541 --> 00:05:00,641
I checked it and froze: "Wait, what?"

117
00:05:00,641 --> 00:05:02,574
Viewers were blindsided.

118
00:05:02,574 --> 00:05:04,541
Everyone lost their minds,

119
00:05:04,541 --> 00:05:06,041
desperately wondering what happens next.

120
00:05:06,041 --> 00:05:07,574
About an eighth pro team...

121
00:05:09,574 --> 00:05:10,441
"Seriously?"

122
00:05:10,807 --> 00:05:13,374
(Season One wrapped on a cliffhanger.)

123
00:05:13,374 --> 00:05:16,174
(- Wait, it ends just like that?
- What kind of finale is this?)

124
00:05:16,174 --> 00:05:18,007
(Is an eighth team really happening?
Or are they teasing Season Two?)

125
00:05:18,007 --> 00:05:21,274
(Buzz around an eighth team reaches
a fever pitch.)

126
00:05:21,974 --> 00:05:23,507
Right? What actually happened?

127
00:05:24,774 --> 00:05:28,141
Today, I'm laying it all out...

128
00:05:28,574 --> 00:05:33,507
everything that unfolded
with corporate sponsors and us...

129
00:05:33,507 --> 00:05:34,907
ever since that broadcast.

130
00:05:34,907 --> 00:05:36,274
- Perfect.
- Nothing held back.

131
00:05:36,274 --> 00:05:38,107
(Behind the scenes
of the bombshell cliffhanger)

132
00:05:38,233 --> 00:05:40,433
- What's that?
- Right after the broadcast wrapped,

133
00:05:40,433 --> 00:05:41,466
my phone rang.

134
00:05:42,033 --> 00:05:44,399
And here is...

135
00:05:45,299 --> 00:05:46,399
the actual recording.

136
00:05:46,933 --> 00:05:49,466
(Actual audio from the phone call)

137
00:05:49,466 --> 00:05:50,399
Hello?

138
00:05:51,133 --> 00:05:52,166
- Hello?
- Hi there.

139
00:05:52,166 --> 00:05:55,133
Hello, I'm calling
from the viewer response center.

140
00:05:55,533 --> 00:05:56,466
Yes?

141
00:05:56,466 --> 00:06:01,666
Are you the lead producer
for The Wonder Coach?

142
00:06:01,666 --> 00:06:02,566
Speaking.

143
00:06:02,566 --> 00:06:06,566
A corporate brand representative...

144
00:06:06,566 --> 00:06:09,166
reached out wanting to explore
founding a volleyball team...

145
00:06:09,166 --> 00:06:11,733
and asked for your direct contact info.

146
00:06:12,533 --> 00:06:13,799
Wait, seriously?

147
00:06:13,799 --> 00:06:16,066
A real company reached out
about launching a franchise.

148
00:06:16,066 --> 00:06:17,033
Right.

149
00:06:17,333 --> 00:06:19,666
And right after that,

150
00:06:19,666 --> 00:06:21,266
- Another one?
- A second company got in touch.

151
00:06:23,733 --> 00:06:24,533
This brand right here.

152
00:06:24,799 --> 00:06:27,166
They were interested
in launching a team too.

153
00:06:28,666 --> 00:06:31,299
Since calls were coming
in the second the finale aired,

154
00:06:31,833 --> 00:06:34,299
we genuinely thought,
"We might actually pull this off."

155
00:06:34,299 --> 00:06:37,999
"The cultural footprint
of this show might just be huge enough."

156
00:06:37,999 --> 00:06:40,099
Discussions were moving along smoothly...

157
00:06:40,666 --> 00:06:41,633
Then early this year,

158
00:06:44,432 --> 00:06:46,633
the war in Iran erupted.

159
00:06:47,666 --> 00:06:49,433
Fears spread
that the conflict would drag out,

160
00:06:49,433 --> 00:06:51,933
sending shockwaves
across the global economy.

161
00:06:51,933 --> 00:06:54,566
Financial markets brace
for the gathering storm.

162
00:06:55,466 --> 00:06:56,999
Once the war broke out in Iran,

163
00:06:56,999 --> 00:07:00,399
- everything froze up...
- Especially for corporations.

164
00:07:00,399 --> 00:07:01,299
Budgets dried up overnight.

165
00:07:01,999 --> 00:07:02,833
On top of that...

166
00:07:03,433 --> 00:07:04,833
another bombshell hit.

167
00:07:05,133 --> 00:07:06,399
The looming shutdown of AI Peppers.

168
00:07:07,399 --> 00:07:11,133
Barely five years in,
AI Peppers faces potential liquidation.

169
00:07:11,566 --> 00:07:13,633
Reports indicate the company will...

170
00:07:13,633 --> 00:07:15,473
essentially pull the plug
on team operations...

171
00:07:15,474 --> 00:07:16,833
amid mounting financial pressure.

172
00:07:17,633 --> 00:07:21,799
- Every brand turned ultra-conservative.
- Makes sense.

173
00:07:21,799 --> 00:07:23,866
Between the war in Iran
and the crisis with AI Peppers,

174
00:07:23,866 --> 00:07:25,633
we were forced to concede...

175
00:07:26,633 --> 00:07:31,566
that entering the league with a new club
this season was out of reach.

176
00:07:36,399 --> 00:07:39,399
Maybe we pitch Seung Kwan instead...

177
00:07:39,399 --> 00:07:41,966
(Owner Boo)

178
00:07:41,966 --> 00:07:42,933
What do you think?
(Bankrolling a pro team on idol money)

179
00:07:44,199 --> 00:07:45,633
He can double as manager and owner.

180
00:07:45,633 --> 00:07:47,399
(Problem solved)

181
00:07:48,133 --> 00:07:51,233
Even through all the chaos,

182
00:07:51,966 --> 00:07:54,566
we did manage to open one serious door.

183
00:07:54,566 --> 00:07:55,333
(Huh?)

184
00:07:58,733 --> 00:07:59,499
What kind of door?

185
00:08:02,366 --> 00:08:07,833
(KOVO, Korea Volleyball Federation)

186
00:08:08,999 --> 00:08:11,433
(Governing body
of the professional volleyball league)

187
00:08:11,933 --> 00:08:14,866
(Overseeing franchises, players,
and match operations)

188
00:08:15,533 --> 00:08:18,566
(Any expansion team requires...)

189
00:08:19,633 --> 00:08:23,399
(formal KOVO clearance.)

190
00:08:23,933 --> 00:08:25,266
(Lee Young Ho, KOVO Secretary General)

191
00:08:25,466 --> 00:08:27,599
(KOVO department heads: Kim Dae Jin,
Jang Kyung Min, Jeon Sang Seok)

192
00:08:29,499 --> 00:08:31,466
We originated
as an unscripted entertainment show.

193
00:08:32,066 --> 00:08:34,566
Do you believe
this can legitimately cross over?

194
00:08:36,366 --> 00:08:38,366
I believe it can.

195
00:08:38,766 --> 00:08:40,099
I really want you guys to pull it off.

196
00:08:40,833 --> 00:08:42,666
I want to see a precedent
like this become reality.

197
00:08:43,499 --> 00:08:45,066
Nothing quite like this has happened...

198
00:08:45,066 --> 00:08:46,333
anywhere across the sports world...

199
00:08:46,333 --> 00:08:48,966
a variety project giving birth
to a sanctioned top-tier pro club.

200
00:08:48,966 --> 00:08:51,866
That very novelty is
why corporations might genuinely bite.

201
00:08:52,833 --> 00:08:55,733
We'll step up and back you however we can.

202
00:08:57,551 --> 00:09:01,685
But they're under a lot of pressure
from the costs.

203
00:09:02,018 --> 00:09:04,651
So we wanted to ask you
how to address this.

204
00:09:05,385 --> 00:09:08,985
It's true that the league's revenue model
has gotten better over the years.

205
00:09:09,351 --> 00:09:11,418
If an enterprise like Kiwoom...

206
00:09:11,418 --> 00:09:14,018
comes in purely
as a naming rights sponsor,

207
00:09:14,318 --> 00:09:15,585
I think that gives us
a real fighting chance.

208
00:09:15,997 --> 00:09:17,850
So if a corporation like Kiwoom...

209
00:09:17,851 --> 00:09:20,118
signs on as a title sponsor...

210
00:09:20,918 --> 00:09:22,551
(A new solution.)

211
00:09:22,551 --> 00:09:25,151
(Naming rights sponsorship.)

212
00:09:25,151 --> 00:09:28,051
The club operates independently
from the corporation,

213
00:09:28,451 --> 00:09:31,285
meaning the sponsor doesn't have
to shoulder all the overhead.

214
00:09:31,285 --> 00:09:32,285
(They fund the franchise
in exchange for naming rights.)

215
00:09:32,618 --> 00:09:34,151
Just like Kiwoom.

216
00:09:34,151 --> 00:09:36,951
- Exactly.
- That's the Kiwoom playbook.

217
00:09:36,951 --> 00:09:38,451
A major corporate sponsorship.

218
00:09:38,451 --> 00:09:41,185
(Kiwoom Securities, the title sponsor)

219
00:09:41,185 --> 00:09:44,718
(Seoul Heroes, the operating club)

220
00:09:44,718 --> 00:09:50,585
("Kiwoom Heroes")

221
00:09:50,918 --> 00:09:54,251
If brands can get prime exposure...

222
00:09:54,418 --> 00:09:56,751
while the club handles its own operations,

223
00:09:57,085 --> 00:09:59,918
they might actually find it
an appealing gamble this season.

224
00:09:59,918 --> 00:10:01,985
That was our thinking.

225
00:10:03,318 --> 00:10:05,385
So we figured...

226
00:10:06,451 --> 00:10:08,485
why couldn't our network run the team?

227
00:10:11,385 --> 00:10:14,918
(MBC is the one running the team?)

228
00:10:14,918 --> 00:10:16,018
(Pilseung Wonder Dogs)

229
00:10:16,018 --> 00:10:19,385
The sponsor gets maximum brand exposure,

230
00:10:19,651 --> 00:10:21,751
while MBC takes on the burden
of running front-office operations.

231
00:10:22,385 --> 00:10:26,085
MBC is actually quite receptive
to the idea.

232
00:10:26,551 --> 00:10:29,318
Either way,
that's a massive commitment for MBC too.

233
00:10:29,318 --> 00:10:31,185
- If they sign off on it.
- Exactly.

234
00:10:32,885 --> 00:10:34,051
Then we're in business.

235
00:10:34,051 --> 00:10:35,451
(We could form a team.)

236
00:10:35,451 --> 00:10:36,451
Here's the thing, though.

237
00:10:36,951 --> 00:10:38,118
Here's my worry.

238
00:10:38,118 --> 00:10:41,651
It's fine and well to launch
a club like this,

239
00:10:41,885 --> 00:10:44,851
but it has to be sustainable
over the long haul.

240
00:10:44,851 --> 00:10:47,118
Look at what happened with AI Peppers.

241
00:10:47,251 --> 00:10:50,085
If the team suddenly folds
after a few years,

242
00:10:50,285 --> 00:10:54,185
these players will just get
their hearts broken all over again,

243
00:10:54,218 --> 00:10:56,685
and they'll have nowhere left to turn.

244
00:10:56,918 --> 00:10:59,151
You mentioned
multiple companies reached out,

245
00:10:59,285 --> 00:11:02,018
but if they're only jumping
in for the PR hype,

246
00:11:02,018 --> 00:11:04,351
just to splash their brand
across the news...

247
00:11:04,351 --> 00:11:07,218
Sure, marketing exposure
is always part of the equation.

248
00:11:07,418 --> 00:11:11,818
Even so, I truly hope whoever signs on...

249
00:11:11,818 --> 00:11:14,851
does it out of genuine care
for these athletes.

250
00:11:15,218 --> 00:11:18,351
You want someone whose passion
for volleyball rivals anyone else's.

251
00:11:18,485 --> 00:11:20,751
Right. People who genuinely care
about the sport.

252
00:11:20,751 --> 00:11:21,951
(Wishing they genuinely care)

253
00:11:22,351 --> 00:11:25,551
What if we prove to them
we're already a pro-caliber squad,

254
00:11:25,985 --> 00:11:28,485
leaving them no reason to say no?

255
00:11:28,485 --> 00:11:31,085
(Let's prove to them
that we can be a pro team.)

256
00:11:31,718 --> 00:11:36,618
Then our mission for Season Two is...

257
00:11:36,785 --> 00:11:40,585
to bring in underdog talent...

258
00:11:40,851 --> 00:11:45,818
and mold them into a league-ready roster.

259
00:11:46,918 --> 00:11:49,985
The game plan is to build a team that's
turnkey and ready to join the pros...

260
00:11:49,985 --> 00:11:52,385
the moment a sponsor backs us.

261
00:11:55,218 --> 00:11:56,218
Man.

262
00:11:56,785 --> 00:11:58,985
I can already feel how grueling...

263
00:11:59,885 --> 00:12:01,051
this whole season is going to be.

264
00:12:01,685 --> 00:12:04,085
I can't keep doing this
for a Season Three or Four.

265
00:12:04,451 --> 00:12:05,451
Seriously.

266
00:12:05,951 --> 00:12:07,951
I don't have that kind of patience.

267
00:12:08,018 --> 00:12:10,751
Which is why if no corporate owner
steps up to claim us,

268
00:12:12,251 --> 00:12:14,485
this season might truly be...

269
00:12:14,951 --> 00:12:17,451
our last and only shot.

270
00:12:17,451 --> 00:12:19,551
So there might not be a Season Three.

271
00:12:19,551 --> 00:12:21,718
We have to operate as if there won't be.

272
00:12:21,718 --> 00:12:23,251
(This is their last chance.)

273
00:12:24,718 --> 00:12:25,912
The odds are completely stacked
against us.

274
00:12:25,913 --> 00:12:29,851
Definitely.
Still, it's worth taking our shot.

275
00:12:29,851 --> 00:12:31,951
(It's worth a try.)

276
00:12:31,951 --> 00:12:34,051
When you aim high,

277
00:12:34,251 --> 00:12:37,451
you might as well shoot for the moon.

278
00:12:37,451 --> 00:12:40,851
"We can pull this off.
Come on, let's make it happen."

279
00:12:40,851 --> 00:12:43,851
That mindset pulls you closer
to the finish line. It gets you there.

280
00:12:45,085 --> 00:12:46,285
We just have to go all in.

281
00:12:47,485 --> 00:12:49,818
I love the sound of that.

282
00:12:49,818 --> 00:12:50,818
(Fascinating.)

283
00:12:50,818 --> 00:12:54,151
So we put together a checklist
of what we need.

284
00:12:54,785 --> 00:12:57,285
For our squad,
it comes down to five essentials.

285
00:12:57,685 --> 00:12:59,251
- First off...
- Upgrade us to luxury coach seats.

286
00:13:00,251 --> 00:13:01,385
(Quickly proposing)

287
00:13:01,385 --> 00:13:03,518
Bus seats these days are incredible.

288
00:13:03,518 --> 00:13:04,785
You can kick your legs all the way up.

289
00:13:05,451 --> 00:13:07,151
- Moving on...
- Right, so...

290
00:13:07,151 --> 00:13:08,618
make that six essentials.

291
00:13:10,618 --> 00:13:13,185
First, we need a dedicated front office.

292
00:13:13,185 --> 00:13:14,985
- Absolutely.
- But we actually have that covered.

293
00:13:15,785 --> 00:13:16,785
Wait, really?

294
00:13:17,351 --> 00:13:20,751
MBC already stood up an operations unit:

295
00:13:21,185 --> 00:13:22,385
"The Wonder Dogs Founding Task Force."

296
00:13:22,585 --> 00:13:23,885
A brand-new division.

297
00:13:23,885 --> 00:13:25,618
They set up an official department right
inside the company.

298
00:13:26,085 --> 00:13:27,985
The internal appointments
came down yesterday.

299
00:13:27,985 --> 00:13:28,985
Take a look at the roster.

300
00:13:30,085 --> 00:13:31,796
They pulled staff
from different departments.

301
00:13:31,797 --> 00:13:32,885
We've got 1, 2, 3, 4...

302
00:13:32,885 --> 00:13:34,851
(A full front office staff,
like an actual team)

303
00:13:35,585 --> 00:13:36,885
So front office: check.

304
00:13:36,885 --> 00:13:38,951
Second on the list is a home city.

305
00:13:38,985 --> 00:13:41,618
A host city. That's another hurdle.

306
00:13:41,951 --> 00:13:45,151
We need an arena for home games,
plus team housing and facilities.

307
00:13:45,251 --> 00:13:48,285
Securing a host city is non-negotiable.

308
00:13:48,718 --> 00:13:51,118
Third, we need corporate backing,
just like we talked about.

309
00:13:51,118 --> 00:13:52,725
A corporate sponsor.
That's priority number one.

310
00:13:52,726 --> 00:13:53,751
The absolute centerpiece.

311
00:13:53,751 --> 00:13:58,185
Then,
to prove this team can draw real numbers,

312
00:13:59,818 --> 00:14:01,285
we could host a live showcase match...

313
00:14:01,585 --> 00:14:03,685
to demonstrate
our drawing power with fans.

314
00:14:04,318 --> 00:14:05,651
And my job will be...

315
00:14:05,651 --> 00:14:07,526
purely dialing in our performance
on the court.

316
00:14:07,527 --> 00:14:08,151
Spot on.

317
00:14:08,385 --> 00:14:10,618
First, a front office.
Second, a home city.

318
00:14:10,618 --> 00:14:12,885
Third, corporate backing.
Fourth, fan attendance.

319
00:14:12,918 --> 00:14:14,751
Fifth, on-court performance.

320
00:14:14,751 --> 00:14:17,051
(Requirements for a pro team
plus a premium bus)

321
00:14:17,485 --> 00:14:20,118
On-court performance feels
like the linchpin.

322
00:14:20,418 --> 00:14:22,585
If we deliver results,
the corporate sponsors will follow,

323
00:14:22,586 --> 00:14:24,151
and so will the fans.

324
00:14:24,618 --> 00:14:28,885
Then there's the roster itself,
the backbone of the whole program.

325
00:14:32,418 --> 00:14:36,151
(Is the lineup good enough?)

326
00:14:36,485 --> 00:14:38,451
The real issue is...

327
00:14:38,918 --> 00:14:40,518
the talent that graduated to the pros.

328
00:14:40,518 --> 00:14:42,618
- We lost so many key players.
- A huge chunk of them.

329
00:14:42,618 --> 00:14:46,251
They were fully pro-ready.

330
00:14:46,485 --> 00:14:49,785
Honestly,
they were the core pillars of our squad.

331
00:14:50,285 --> 00:14:51,951
Losing them was a massive blow.

332
00:14:55,085 --> 00:14:56,485
We took a major hit to our depth.

333
00:14:56,485 --> 00:14:59,118
(Key players lost)

334
00:14:59,385 --> 00:15:01,218
We're in full crisis mode.

335
00:15:03,218 --> 00:15:07,085
(The Wonder Dogs' shift
from glory to a crisis)

336
00:15:07,285 --> 00:15:09,618
We're facing an uphill battle.

337
00:15:09,618 --> 00:15:12,318
It's been a whole year,

338
00:15:12,818 --> 00:15:14,685
so their physical conditioning might have
dropped off...

339
00:15:14,685 --> 00:15:16,351
along with their match sharpness.

340
00:15:17,485 --> 00:15:20,251
A year away is an eternity in sports.

341
00:15:20,285 --> 00:15:22,185
(Have they changed significantly?)

342
00:15:22,385 --> 00:15:25,018
- Myoung Hwa went down with an injury.
- Right.

343
00:15:25,018 --> 00:15:27,185
Her knees and multiple spots.

344
00:15:27,951 --> 00:15:31,918
("Injury After Another!
Moon Myoung Hwa Suffers Knee Injuries.")

345
00:15:34,451 --> 00:15:37,051
(Unable to join due to injury)

346
00:15:37,051 --> 00:15:39,751
And Na Hee went down as well.

347
00:15:39,751 --> 00:15:41,451
(Kim Na Hee, injured)

348
00:15:43,451 --> 00:15:46,051
(Kim Hyeon Jeong, injured)

349
00:15:47,018 --> 00:15:49,118
(All the middle blockers...)

350
00:15:49,118 --> 00:15:51,451
(are unable to join the team.)

351
00:15:51,751 --> 00:15:55,518
On top of that, several players...

352
00:15:55,851 --> 00:15:58,351
stepped away to start new careers.

353
00:15:58,351 --> 00:15:59,351
(Those who left the court?)

354
00:15:59,351 --> 00:16:00,785
Random two!

355
00:16:02,951 --> 00:16:04,618
Hold! All right.

356
00:16:04,618 --> 00:16:06,885
(Choi Su Bin now works
at a sports-related organization.)

357
00:16:07,451 --> 00:16:11,618
(Tamira has taken a new path
after retiring due to injury.)

358
00:16:12,785 --> 00:16:15,151
(Gaps left by players turning pro)

359
00:16:15,851 --> 00:16:18,318
(Sidelined by injuries)

360
00:16:19,085 --> 00:16:21,551
(Players who chose a new path)

361
00:16:24,451 --> 00:16:28,185
(A severe loss for the team)

362
00:16:30,085 --> 00:16:34,318
We're walking into this season
in rougher shape...

363
00:16:34,651 --> 00:16:36,018
than when we first started Season One.

364
00:16:38,051 --> 00:16:39,885
We're supposed to be taking
a step forward,

365
00:16:40,185 --> 00:16:42,718
yet piecing together a competitive roster
has gotten ten times harder.

366
00:16:44,218 --> 00:16:45,218
Tell me about it.

367
00:16:46,718 --> 00:16:50,318
(Facing a crisis from the start)

368
00:16:51,885 --> 00:16:55,285
It's going to be brutal,
but we have to field a squad.

369
00:16:55,518 --> 00:16:57,285
We need a roster that can actually
get the job done.

370
00:16:57,785 --> 00:16:59,518
We'll just have to adjust on the fly.

371
00:16:59,551 --> 00:17:00,651
(Coach Kim's masterstroke)

372
00:17:00,685 --> 00:17:03,985
An upgraded open tryout. That's our move.

373
00:17:04,918 --> 00:17:08,551
(Tryout:
a field test to find the best players)

374
00:17:08,551 --> 00:17:09,651
("Recruitment Notice")

375
00:17:09,651 --> 00:17:13,218
(Began to recruit players for the tryout)

376
00:17:13,218 --> 00:17:15,351
("Corporate team, retired players,
and rising talents.")

377
00:17:15,351 --> 00:17:17,651
("All are welcome!")

378
00:17:21,951 --> 00:17:26,385
(A bigger wave of applicants
than in the first season)

379
00:17:27,218 --> 00:17:29,585
Hello, everyone. Great to see you.

380
00:17:29,951 --> 00:17:32,785
(A virtual meeting of the coaching staff)

381
00:17:32,851 --> 00:17:35,351
I'll map out the entire itinerary
and run the sessions.

382
00:17:35,985 --> 00:17:39,885
(The rookie coach leads the meeting.)

383
00:17:40,385 --> 00:17:41,385
(June)

384
00:17:41,718 --> 00:17:43,451
(A few days later,
Coach Kim suddenly calls.)

385
00:17:43,451 --> 00:17:45,251
We need to talk face-to-face.

386
00:17:45,251 --> 00:17:49,151
(Emergency coaching staff meeting)

387
00:17:49,885 --> 00:17:52,518
(The second meeting of the coaching staff)

388
00:17:52,518 --> 00:17:55,118
Let's lock down who owns which roles.

389
00:17:55,118 --> 00:17:57,718
(Also reviewing the plan
and the people in charge)

390
00:17:57,718 --> 00:17:59,985
I think this covers all our bases for now.

391
00:17:59,985 --> 00:18:01,085
Looks solid.

392
00:18:03,018 --> 00:18:08,451
(The day of the tryout)

393
00:18:27,251 --> 00:18:31,151
(All lined up by position.)

394
00:18:32,851 --> 00:18:34,318
What's with the energy in here?

395
00:18:35,285 --> 00:18:36,951
Why is everyone so on edge?

396
00:18:36,951 --> 00:18:38,131
(Chae Seon Ah)

397
00:18:38,131 --> 00:18:40,218
(Three-time V-League champion,
343 games, 542 points)

398
00:18:40,651 --> 00:18:42,718
I had no idea Seon Ah was showing up.

399
00:18:43,318 --> 00:18:44,328
(Kim Da Sol)

400
00:18:44,329 --> 00:18:45,951
(Two-time V-League champion,
played 240 games)

401
00:18:46,285 --> 00:18:48,818
I just spotted Sang Mi in the gym.

402
00:18:49,151 --> 00:18:51,951
Sang Mi being here caught me
completely off guard.

403
00:18:52,518 --> 00:18:55,185
I couldn't believe my eyes
when I saw Sang Mi.

404
00:18:55,185 --> 00:18:56,717
(Park Sang Mi: Jung Kwan Jang,
Altos, Pink Spiders)

405
00:18:57,131 --> 00:19:00,074
Honestly, seeing starting liberos
from the corporate league show up,

406
00:19:00,588 --> 00:19:04,288
I figured my chances were even slimmer.

407
00:19:04,554 --> 00:19:06,254
(Daegu City Hall's starting libero)

408
00:19:06,621 --> 00:19:08,554
Wait, is that a Japanese player?

409
00:19:09,221 --> 00:19:11,154
There were no nationality limits.

410
00:19:13,054 --> 00:19:16,354
(Tanyama Tsubaki: Japan U18 national team,
Asian U18 Best Setter)

411
00:19:17,021 --> 00:19:19,021
(Ha Hyo Rim: Asian Youth national team,
U18 World Championship squad)

412
00:19:19,688 --> 00:19:21,788
(Park Hyeon Ju: First second-round draft
pick to win V-League Rookie of the Year)

413
00:19:22,554 --> 00:19:27,088
I'm Ji Min Kyeong, an outside hitter
formerly with Hillstate.

414
00:19:29,088 --> 00:19:31,321
I parted ways with Hillstate...

415
00:19:31,854 --> 00:19:35,088
before I ever got a real chance
to show what I can do.

416
00:19:35,388 --> 00:19:37,021
(Ji Min Kyeong: 2017 V-League ROY,
Asian U17 national team selection)

417
00:19:37,259 --> 00:19:40,454
(Ji Min Kyeong:
waived by Hillstate in 2026)

418
00:19:40,654 --> 00:19:43,488
I'm a free agent right now.

419
00:19:43,488 --> 00:19:44,554
(Kim Da Sol:
waived by Pink Spiders in 2026)

420
00:19:45,421 --> 00:19:47,854
I currently play
for the Pohang City Athletic Association.

421
00:19:47,854 --> 00:19:48,821
(Chae Seon Ah:
waived by AI Peppers in 2025)

422
00:19:48,821 --> 00:19:50,554
(Park Hyeon Ju:
waived by Pink Spiders in 2024)

423
00:19:50,554 --> 00:19:52,321
(An Ye Rim: waived by Red Sparks in 2026)

424
00:19:52,321 --> 00:19:54,188
(Lee Ho Bin: waived by Red Sparks in 2026)

425
00:19:54,188 --> 00:19:55,854
(Woo Su Min: waived by KIXX in 2026)

426
00:19:55,854 --> 00:19:57,354
(Kim Chae Na:
waived by Red Sparks in 2026)

427
00:19:57,354 --> 00:19:58,888
(Jo Bo Yun: waived by Hillstate in 2026)

428
00:19:59,454 --> 00:20:01,488
(Amid the wave of former pro veterans,)

429
00:20:02,054 --> 00:20:04,954
(two familiar faces catch everyone's eye.)

430
00:20:05,421 --> 00:20:08,788
The outside hitters are putting
on a clinic with their attacking power.

431
00:20:08,788 --> 00:20:09,754
Kim Yoon Ha.

432
00:20:10,188 --> 00:20:12,454
(Kim Yoon Ha: undrafted in 2025)

433
00:20:12,888 --> 00:20:14,288
(After facing the Wonder Dogs,)

434
00:20:15,354 --> 00:20:17,121
(Oh Eun Chae was drafted by AI Peppers.)

435
00:20:17,121 --> 00:20:18,954
I stayed on the roster for one season,

436
00:20:19,254 --> 00:20:21,721
and then they let me go.

437
00:20:23,688 --> 00:20:26,221
I never even saw the floor
for my pro debut,

438
00:20:26,221 --> 00:20:27,088
so to be honest...

439
00:20:30,554 --> 00:20:31,588
it stung pretty badly.

440
00:20:44,921 --> 00:20:46,654
Even after getting cut,

441
00:20:46,654 --> 00:20:50,088
giving up on volleyball never once
crossed my mind.

442
00:20:50,088 --> 00:20:52,554
It made me tougher.

443
00:20:52,954 --> 00:20:57,921
When I played against the Wonder Dogs
back in high school,

444
00:20:57,921 --> 00:21:03,521
I didn't get how anyone could
be that desperate.

445
00:21:04,454 --> 00:21:10,254
(Back then, that sheer desperation
didn't register.)

446
00:21:10,854 --> 00:21:15,088
After turning pro and getting cut myself,
though,

447
00:21:15,088 --> 00:21:18,154
I finally understood what those
older players were going through.

448
00:21:18,154 --> 00:21:20,288
Putting myself in their shoes,

449
00:21:20,288 --> 00:21:23,288
I looked back at how hard they battled
and screamed for every point.

450
00:21:23,788 --> 00:21:29,421
They laid it all on the line
because they wanted that win so badly.

451
00:21:31,654 --> 00:21:34,821
More than anything,
I came here to prove I belong.

452
00:21:35,954 --> 00:21:38,421
I left the pro circuit with so much
left on the table,

453
00:21:38,421 --> 00:21:41,421
and I want to show what I'm truly made of.

454
00:21:42,154 --> 00:21:46,321
I still dream of earning a starting spot
in the pros.

455
00:21:46,721 --> 00:21:50,521
It's a dream I refuse to let go of.

456
00:21:50,888 --> 00:21:53,721
I want to take this head-on
and see if I can break through.

457
00:21:54,121 --> 00:21:57,321
I'm treating this like my final stop.

458
00:21:58,321 --> 00:22:01,688
If I miss this shot, I'm done.
So I'm laying everything on the line.

459
00:22:20,288 --> 00:22:22,854
(Koo Hye In, Enkhsoyol:
Season One Wonder Dog)

460
00:22:25,388 --> 00:22:28,192
(Baek Chae Rim, Han Song Hee:
Season One Wonder Dog)

461
00:22:30,688 --> 00:22:33,388
(Lee Jin, Yoon Young In:
Season One Wonder Dog)

462
00:22:38,154 --> 00:22:39,188
I definitely didn't see that coming.

463
00:22:39,721 --> 00:22:41,588
My first reaction was,
"Wait, why are they back?"

464
00:22:42,088 --> 00:22:43,621
I was floored to see them walking in too.

465
00:22:43,621 --> 00:22:45,988
My thought was,
"They're really running it back."

466
00:22:45,988 --> 00:22:47,754
(A veteran coach's cold calculus)

467
00:22:48,254 --> 00:22:51,088
I think we have to evaluate them
from scratch.

468
00:22:51,088 --> 00:22:53,121
- Every single one of them?
- Yes.

469
00:22:53,121 --> 00:22:54,354
(Firm)

470
00:22:55,021 --> 00:22:56,954
- The pro game is cutthroat.
- Spot on.

471
00:22:57,454 --> 00:23:00,321
As far as I know, Enkhsoyol...

472
00:23:00,321 --> 00:23:02,088
barely saw any floor time...

473
00:23:02,088 --> 00:23:05,188
after signing with Red Sparks.

474
00:23:05,391 --> 00:23:07,421
Her match conditioning is definitely
a question mark.

475
00:23:07,421 --> 00:23:10,321
Enkhsoyol has joined Red Sparks.

476
00:23:10,588 --> 00:23:11,621
("Enkhsoyol Fever Sells Out
Red Sparks Home Opener")

477
00:23:11,621 --> 00:23:12,788
("Kim Yeon Koung's Protégé Enkhsoyol
Turns Pro with Red Sparks")

478
00:23:12,788 --> 00:23:14,388
("The Enkhsoyol Effect Delivers
Another Sellout Crowd")

479
00:23:15,488 --> 00:23:19,454
(A stress fracture
derails her pro campaign.)

480
00:23:20,354 --> 00:23:23,554
(Sidelined by a lingering injury)

481
00:23:25,021 --> 00:23:28,888
(Her pro stint cut short.)

482
00:23:29,321 --> 00:23:31,621
(Enkhsoyol returns
to Mokpo Science University.)

483
00:23:31,854 --> 00:23:33,428
Athletes need live match reps
to stay sharp,

484
00:23:33,429 --> 00:23:35,821
and she hasn't seen real court time
in a while.

485
00:23:35,821 --> 00:23:37,588
That's what worries me.

486
00:23:38,154 --> 00:23:42,221
Several players who suited up
for the Wonder Dogs last season...

487
00:23:42,221 --> 00:23:43,988
went back to their corporate clubs...

488
00:23:43,988 --> 00:23:45,588
only to ride the bench.

489
00:23:47,154 --> 00:23:50,321
(Koo Hye In:
bench reserve at Suwon Special City)

490
00:23:50,954 --> 00:23:54,154
(Lee Jin:
bench reserve at Daegu City Hall)

491
00:23:55,221 --> 00:24:00,688
Players have to get consistent match reps
to hone their craft and stay sharp.

492
00:24:01,154 --> 00:24:02,921
Step away for just a month or two,

493
00:24:02,921 --> 00:24:05,354
and getting back to peak game form
is an uphill battle.

494
00:24:05,721 --> 00:24:08,621
Now that an entire year has gone by,

495
00:24:09,021 --> 00:24:12,921
we really have to run them
through full evaluations again.

496
00:24:12,921 --> 00:24:15,021
What's the point of grading them
on how they played a year ago?

497
00:24:15,021 --> 00:24:16,754
I was putting up MVP numbers
two years ago too.

498
00:24:16,754 --> 00:24:19,821
I took home V-League MVP two years ago,
for that matter.

499
00:24:21,454 --> 00:24:23,154
Looking at it like that,

500
00:24:23,154 --> 00:24:25,588
we genuinely have to wipe the slate clean.

501
00:24:32,254 --> 00:24:34,888
(The Season One Wonder Dogs return
across the board.)

502
00:24:34,888 --> 00:24:37,854
I knew I had what it takes
to make the cut.

503
00:24:38,154 --> 00:24:39,854
Backing down wasn't an option.

504
00:24:40,221 --> 00:24:42,121
Confidence was never the issue.

505
00:24:42,121 --> 00:24:46,321
My mindset was that I had
to outperform everyone else out there.

506
00:24:47,154 --> 00:24:49,788
I couldn't let down the Wonder Dogs' name.

507
00:24:51,754 --> 00:24:53,221
I knew it was going
to be an uphill battle.

508
00:24:58,354 --> 00:25:01,554
(Head Coach Kim Yeon Koung)

509
00:25:08,221 --> 00:25:11,954
(Anchored by an elite coaching staff)

510
00:25:15,188 --> 00:25:16,021
Hey there.

511
00:25:16,921 --> 00:25:17,988
Quite the crowd this year.

512
00:25:19,054 --> 00:25:20,921
(The Wonder Dogs' beefed-up
coaching staff)

513
00:25:22,254 --> 00:25:25,288
I'm Yoon Bong Woo,
coaching for the Pilseung Wonder Dogs.

514
00:25:26,554 --> 00:25:27,921
(Coach Yoon Bong Woo)

515
00:25:27,921 --> 00:25:29,188
(Former national team
starting middle blocker)

516
00:25:29,188 --> 00:25:30,454
(2006 Doha Asian Games gold medalist)

517
00:25:30,454 --> 00:25:31,621
Swing with conviction.

518
00:25:31,621 --> 00:25:33,021
You have to keep testing that line...

519
00:25:33,021 --> 00:25:34,921
to learn how to paint
that spot with the ball.

520
00:25:35,721 --> 00:25:38,354
Hold your ground, and you take the point.
Stand tall.

521
00:25:39,121 --> 00:25:40,921
We're pushing you like this
because we know what you're capable of.

522
00:25:42,221 --> 00:25:46,354
(A trusted mentor for the players)

523
00:25:47,121 --> 00:25:49,388
I'm Lee Hyo Hee,
setter coach for the Wonder Dogs.

524
00:25:50,754 --> 00:25:51,888
(Coach Lee Hyo Hee)

525
00:25:51,888 --> 00:25:52,954
(Former national team setter)

526
00:25:52,954 --> 00:25:53,954
(2014 Incheon Asian Games gold medalist)

527
00:25:53,954 --> 00:25:55,612
Make sure you actually
understand the concept.

528
00:25:55,613 --> 00:25:56,821
Don't just nod your head and say yes.

529
00:25:56,821 --> 00:25:58,754
You're falling behind the pace out here.

530
00:25:59,154 --> 00:26:01,621
(A disarming smile, blunt home truths)

531
00:26:01,621 --> 00:26:02,788
Are your eyes even on the block?

532
00:26:03,488 --> 00:26:05,588
Read the block when you run your drills.

533
00:26:05,921 --> 00:26:08,021
Shake it off.
Seal the seam! Close it down!

534
00:26:08,021 --> 00:26:09,254
Don't turn your body away!

535
00:26:09,754 --> 00:26:11,121
Square up and dig the ball!

536
00:26:11,121 --> 00:26:12,088
Quicker! Keep moving!

537
00:26:12,854 --> 00:26:14,021
(Things can get heated.)

538
00:26:14,021 --> 00:26:15,121
Why are you diving on that?

539
00:26:15,121 --> 00:26:16,188
Are you trying to show off
for the cameras?

540
00:26:16,621 --> 00:26:17,688
Play the ball, don't play to the crowd.

541
00:26:18,054 --> 00:26:20,688
(The squad's resident hard-nosed critic)

542
00:26:20,854 --> 00:26:23,929
Standard pro clubs run
three or four coaches.

543
00:26:23,930 --> 00:26:24,954
We have five.

544
00:26:25,754 --> 00:26:29,888
We significantly expanded
our coaching staff compared to last year.

545
00:26:29,888 --> 00:26:32,788
We also brought on additional medical and
training staff to keep everyone healthy.

546
00:26:33,454 --> 00:26:35,054
(Scouting the talent...)

547
00:26:35,621 --> 00:26:41,688
(who can elevate the Wonder Dogs
to the next tier)

548
00:26:42,254 --> 00:26:44,688
Has everyone seen the tryout order?

549
00:26:46,421 --> 00:26:48,688
(Position-by-position tryouts)

550
00:26:49,654 --> 00:26:52,588
(Intensive evaluations
by the coaching staff,)

551
00:26:53,321 --> 00:26:56,321
(backed by analytics
and biomechanical data)

552
00:26:56,321 --> 00:26:57,821
(Tryout: Outside Hitter Evaluation Sheet)

553
00:27:00,121 --> 00:27:01,188
(Skill assessment)

554
00:27:01,188 --> 00:27:02,021
(Position-specific testing metrics)

555
00:27:02,021 --> 00:27:03,488
(Tryout: Opposite Hitter Evaluation Sheet)

556
00:27:03,488 --> 00:27:05,188
(Tryout: Setter Evaluation Sheet)

557
00:27:05,188 --> 00:27:06,854
(Tryout: Libero Evaluation Sheet)

558
00:27:06,854 --> 00:27:08,488
(Tryout: Middle Blocker Evaluation Sheet)

559
00:27:09,054 --> 00:27:10,554
Her fundamentals are rock solid.

560
00:27:10,954 --> 00:27:12,888
She has great upside as an attacker.
Always looking to put the ball away.

561
00:27:13,088 --> 00:27:14,254
Her touch on the ball can get erratic.

562
00:27:15,054 --> 00:27:17,254
(Minus 1 for Game management)

563
00:27:17,254 --> 00:27:19,088
We wanted to run a few more tests,

564
00:27:19,088 --> 00:27:20,854
so we broadened the evaluation battery.

565
00:27:20,854 --> 00:27:21,862
(Hang time)

566
00:27:21,863 --> 00:27:22,806
It's 285.

567
00:27:23,521 --> 00:27:25,388
(Vertical leap)

568
00:27:25,995 --> 00:27:27,828
(Serve velocity)

569
00:27:28,761 --> 00:27:29,771
(Set release speed)

570
00:27:30,554 --> 00:27:34,788
(Screenings to mitigate injury risk)

571
00:27:36,221 --> 00:27:38,221
(Time to see what they brought)

572
00:27:38,821 --> 00:27:41,021
- Everyone good and warm?
- Yes!

573
00:27:41,021 --> 00:27:42,421
(First position on the floor)

574
00:27:43,454 --> 00:27:46,188
(Outside hitters: The engine of the squad)

575
00:27:47,721 --> 00:27:52,088
(Two-way anchors responsible
for both attack and reception)

576
00:27:52,554 --> 00:27:53,354
All right.

577
00:27:53,754 --> 00:27:55,354
You just hoisted the trophy, right?

578
00:27:55,354 --> 00:27:56,521
Congratulations on the title.

579
00:27:56,521 --> 00:27:57,921
And thank you for coming out.

580
00:27:58,754 --> 00:28:02,688
This season, our system revolves around...

581
00:28:02,688 --> 00:28:06,088
a much faster,
more dynamic brand of volleyball.

582
00:28:06,088 --> 00:28:08,921
I want to see
if you can execute at that tempo.

583
00:28:09,788 --> 00:28:13,854
(Pinpoint first pass right to the setter)

584
00:28:14,482 --> 00:28:16,282
Under one second. Get the ball
out of your hands in under a second.

585
00:28:16,588 --> 00:28:19,888
(Setting within one second
to run tempo attacks)

586
00:28:22,188 --> 00:28:23,954
(First up:
Season One veteran Han Song Hee)

587
00:28:24,221 --> 00:28:25,888
Ready!

588
00:28:26,888 --> 00:28:29,288
(Digs the ball,)

589
00:28:29,288 --> 00:28:30,921
(then transitions to put it down)

590
00:28:31,854 --> 00:28:32,754
Hey!

591
00:28:33,254 --> 00:28:34,221
Quicker to the ball!

592
00:28:35,321 --> 00:28:37,521
(Next up:
Season One veteran Baek Chae Rim)

593
00:28:40,688 --> 00:28:42,354
(Can she deliver?)

594
00:28:42,354 --> 00:28:44,221
Quicker!

595
00:28:44,888 --> 00:28:46,521
(Zero room for compromise)

596
00:28:46,721 --> 00:28:47,988
How much faster are we
supposed to push it?

597
00:28:50,488 --> 00:28:52,721
Having Coach Kim glaring down from
right behind the baseline,

598
00:28:53,288 --> 00:28:55,154
it was definitely intimidating.

599
00:28:55,390 --> 00:28:58,040
The coach is like a hawk.

600
00:28:58,091 --> 00:29:01,427
Instead of talking, she just tracks
everything with laser focus.

601
00:29:01,828 --> 00:29:02,961
She was dialed in like that all day.

602
00:29:03,063 --> 00:29:06,232
Barely saying a word,
just taking mental notes.

603
00:29:09,903 --> 00:29:12,172
(Eagle vision)

604
00:29:12,173 --> 00:29:14,240
Honestly, that silence made it
ten times more nerve-racking.

605
00:29:15,108 --> 00:29:15,908
Ready.

606
00:29:15,909 --> 00:29:16,942
(Former professional player Song Eun Chae)

607
00:29:16,943 --> 00:29:17,810
Perfect.

608
00:29:19,446 --> 00:29:22,048
(Watching intently)

609
00:29:25,719 --> 00:29:27,353
(Song Eun Chae: minus 1 for receive)

610
00:29:29,422 --> 00:29:30,689
(Hmm...)

611
00:29:30,690 --> 00:29:31,690
Missed it?

612
00:29:32,692 --> 00:29:35,527
(Hawk-Eyed Coach zeroing in on every flaw)

613
00:29:35,995 --> 00:29:36,795
(The pressure mounts)
Dig it!

614
00:29:44,170 --> 00:29:45,003
Pass!

615
00:29:45,305 --> 00:29:46,138
Let's work!

616
00:29:46,139 --> 00:29:47,206
(Lee Chae Min: minus 1 for receive)

617
00:29:47,475 --> 00:29:48,374
Dig it!

618
00:29:48,875 --> 00:29:51,310
(Ji Min Kyeong, another former pro)

619
00:29:51,913 --> 00:29:53,713
Mine!

620
00:29:54,214 --> 00:29:56,148
(Ji Min Kyeong: minus 1 for receive)

621
00:29:56,549 --> 00:29:57,682
(Ji Min Kyeong: minus 1 for attack)

622
00:29:57,683 --> 00:29:58,583
Run it back.

623
00:29:58,785 --> 00:29:59,585
Run it back.

624
00:30:00,954 --> 00:30:01,720
Shoot.

625
00:30:02,255 --> 00:30:03,756
(Ji Min Kyeong: minus 2 for receive)

626
00:30:03,757 --> 00:30:05,124
My legs feel heavy.

627
00:30:06,059 --> 00:30:08,494
Why is it so hard to find an OH
who can actually pass the ball?

628
00:30:09,195 --> 00:30:10,028
Hit it.

629
00:30:10,897 --> 00:30:12,531
Hold up.

630
00:30:15,168 --> 00:30:18,237
When the ball has that much pace on it,

631
00:30:18,571 --> 00:30:20,902
if you start all the way back here,
you'll never catch up to it.

632
00:30:21,675 --> 00:30:22,842
You need to set up right here.

633
00:30:23,143 --> 00:30:24,877
Your base has to be here.

634
00:30:24,878 --> 00:30:27,447
That's your only shot at cutting off
a ball coming in that hot.

635
00:30:27,448 --> 00:30:29,014
- Okay.
- Don't drift too deep.

636
00:30:29,015 --> 00:30:30,983
Just a word of advice.

637
00:30:30,984 --> 00:30:31,851
(Can they adjust?)

638
00:30:32,952 --> 00:30:34,386
(Evaluation resumes.)

639
00:30:34,387 --> 00:30:36,021
Got it!

640
00:30:37,323 --> 00:30:38,456
(Lee Chae Min: plus 1 for receive)

641
00:30:39,292 --> 00:30:41,560
(Drifting over the line?)

642
00:30:45,665 --> 00:30:49,401
(So locked in on the pass,)

643
00:30:49,402 --> 00:30:52,437
(she creeps right across the line.)

644
00:30:53,139 --> 00:30:54,539
I literally just told them not
to drift back, and look at her.

645
00:30:55,943 --> 00:30:57,310
(Wonder Dogs Season One veteran,
Baek Chae Rim, steps up.)

646
00:30:57,311 --> 00:30:58,310
Over here!

647
00:31:01,249 --> 00:31:02,081
(Baek Chae Rim: plus 1 for receive)

648
00:31:02,082 --> 00:31:03,149
Her mechanics are clean.

649
00:31:07,420 --> 00:31:09,020
(Baek Chae Rim: plus 1 for attack)

650
00:31:10,223 --> 00:31:11,425
(Executing the fundamentals to perfection)

651
00:31:11,426 --> 00:31:12,791
Nice!

652
00:31:13,193 --> 00:31:15,995
See that touch?
That's textbook right there.

653
00:31:17,063 --> 00:31:19,131
(Riding the wave of Chae Rim's
momentum...)

654
00:31:19,399 --> 00:31:20,299
Step up!

655
00:31:20,300 --> 00:31:21,667
(Enkhsoyol from Wonder Dogs Season One)

656
00:31:22,869 --> 00:31:24,703
I heard she was completely shut down...

657
00:31:24,704 --> 00:31:27,973
for over two months
with a stress fracture.

658
00:31:28,474 --> 00:31:33,078
(Carrying a lingering foot issue...)

659
00:31:33,280 --> 00:31:36,748
I was worried about whether she could
even move at full speed today.

660
00:31:37,350 --> 00:31:38,116
Go!

661
00:31:38,952 --> 00:31:39,885
Ready!

662
00:31:40,019 --> 00:31:40,785
Toss!

663
00:31:41,755 --> 00:31:42,588
(Enkhsoyol: plus 1 for receive)

664
00:31:43,089 --> 00:31:43,889
Good.

665
00:31:44,290 --> 00:31:45,156
Service!

666
00:31:45,157 --> 00:31:47,525
(Full sprint down the line)

667
00:31:48,895 --> 00:31:52,364
The timing on that approach was lethal.

668
00:31:52,432 --> 00:31:54,266
Great cut!

669
00:31:54,267 --> 00:31:55,701
(Enkhsoyol: plus 1 for attack)

670
00:31:55,702 --> 00:31:58,070
I walked in feeling uneasy,

671
00:31:58,071 --> 00:32:01,774
but I was determined to prove
how much I've evolved since Season One.

672
00:32:02,308 --> 00:32:03,208
Service!

673
00:32:04,745 --> 00:32:05,710
Go!

674
00:32:06,813 --> 00:32:08,681
(No longer the passive Yes-khsoyol)

675
00:32:09,148 --> 00:32:10,281
(Locked in)

676
00:32:11,584 --> 00:32:12,517
That's it!

677
00:32:14,287 --> 00:32:15,153
She's good.

678
00:32:17,991 --> 00:32:20,059
She mentioned she didn't get
nearly enough reps in camp.

679
00:32:20,060 --> 00:32:22,094
Yet her game shape looks way
better than expected.

680
00:32:22,095 --> 00:32:22,861
Go!

681
00:32:23,763 --> 00:32:24,963
(Smiles)

682
00:32:26,232 --> 00:32:27,165
I've got it!

683
00:32:28,768 --> 00:32:30,335
(Meanwhile, someone is quietly
chasing down stray balls.)

684
00:32:31,004 --> 00:32:31,904
Enkhsoyol is playing on another level.

685
00:32:31,905 --> 00:32:34,239
You can feel the difference, right?

686
00:32:34,240 --> 00:32:36,175
(Manager Boo grinding behind the scenes)

687
00:32:37,010 --> 00:32:37,910
Over here!

688
00:32:37,911 --> 00:32:38,978
(Han Song Hee,
another Season One Wonder Dog)

689
00:32:39,646 --> 00:32:40,546
Go!

690
00:32:41,414 --> 00:32:42,781
(Han Song Hee: plus 1 for receive)

691
00:32:43,216 --> 00:32:44,183
Put it away!

692
00:32:45,985 --> 00:32:47,185
Huge!

693
00:32:47,186 --> 00:32:48,253
(Han Song Hee: plus 1 for attack)

694
00:32:48,555 --> 00:32:50,388
Great rip, Song Hee!

695
00:32:50,389 --> 00:32:51,323
(Song Hee puts it away with ease)

696
00:32:51,324 --> 00:32:52,991
Song Hee's vertical is unreal.

697
00:32:55,162 --> 00:32:56,695
She has enough hang time to eat
a bowl of ramyun up there.

698
00:32:56,996 --> 00:32:57,862
Nice!

699
00:32:59,233 --> 00:33:01,433
Her conditioning looks incredible.

700
00:33:03,236 --> 00:33:05,070
(The pocket powerhouse returns
with even more juice.)

701
00:33:05,204 --> 00:33:07,273
Song Hee is in great shape.

702
00:33:07,274 --> 00:33:08,307
There's real heat behind that swing.

703
00:33:09,676 --> 00:33:11,043
Look at that pace.

704
00:33:11,044 --> 00:33:12,210
(Han Song Hee: plus 3 for attack)

705
00:33:12,211 --> 00:33:13,345
That Season One run
with the Wonder Dogs...

706
00:33:13,780 --> 00:33:16,081
definitely left its mark on them.

707
00:33:16,082 --> 00:33:18,283
(Season One Wonder Dogs put on a clinic.)

708
00:33:18,284 --> 00:33:21,120
You just can't buy
that kind of game experience.

709
00:33:22,989 --> 00:33:25,057
(Coach Hawk's stern face...)

710
00:33:25,558 --> 00:33:29,861
(is softened by the former
Wonder Dogs' performance.)

711
00:33:31,016 --> 00:33:34,018
She took a massive leap compared
to last year.

712
00:33:34,033 --> 00:33:35,000
(While the Season One outside hitters
run the floor,)

713
00:33:35,802 --> 00:33:38,570
(another Season One veteran takes
center stage.)

714
00:33:38,938 --> 00:33:40,939
(Setter Lee Jin)

715
00:33:41,808 --> 00:33:42,608
(Thwack)

716
00:33:43,276 --> 00:33:45,043
(The ball flies across the court.)

717
00:33:45,044 --> 00:33:46,044
There it is!

718
00:33:47,780 --> 00:33:48,747
Sweet release!

719
00:33:49,283 --> 00:33:50,282
Smooth!

720
00:33:50,850 --> 00:33:51,750
That was butter.

721
00:33:52,485 --> 00:33:55,220
She's got real power.

722
00:33:57,124 --> 00:33:59,824
The setter is the absolute heartbeat
of the floor.

723
00:34:00,893 --> 00:34:05,764
(The setter: floor general of the court)

724
00:34:06,399 --> 00:34:10,168
(Directing the offensive flow)

725
00:34:10,169 --> 00:34:11,803
Setters will block the net first,

726
00:34:11,804 --> 00:34:12,838
(Setter testing)

727
00:34:13,073 --> 00:34:16,508
then peel off and set.
Block, then deliver.

728
00:34:16,509 --> 00:34:18,510
(Back-row distance set)

729
00:34:21,047 --> 00:34:23,248
(Missing the mark over and over)

730
00:34:23,249 --> 00:34:24,182
Ah.

731
00:34:26,619 --> 00:34:27,752
That's not carrying the distance.

732
00:34:27,753 --> 00:34:31,122
(Tough to push that deep
with standard arm strength)

733
00:34:31,824 --> 00:34:32,724
Gosh.

734
00:34:33,860 --> 00:34:35,728
(Stepping up next: Lee Jin...)

735
00:34:39,532 --> 00:34:40,532
Go!

736
00:34:40,900 --> 00:34:43,969
(Lee Jin: plus 1 for long set)

737
00:34:43,970 --> 00:34:46,404
(Lee Jin: plus 2 for long set)

738
00:34:46,405 --> 00:34:48,173
(Lee Jin: plus 3 for long set)

739
00:34:50,209 --> 00:34:52,477
She generates so much power effortlessly.

740
00:34:53,546 --> 00:34:55,881
(Beaming with pride)

741
00:34:57,250 --> 00:34:59,551
Jin pushes high balls with ease!

742
00:34:59,552 --> 00:35:00,452
She's good.

743
00:35:00,853 --> 00:35:03,655
She completely blew my expectations
out of the water.

744
00:35:03,656 --> 00:35:05,223
That's why she made the squad
last time around.

745
00:35:05,593 --> 00:35:07,626
I think I've changed my mind.

746
00:35:07,627 --> 00:35:09,661
Told you so.

747
00:35:09,662 --> 00:35:11,630
Truthfully, I had my doubts coming in.

748
00:35:11,631 --> 00:35:14,700
So seeing our Season One Wonder Dogs...

749
00:35:14,701 --> 00:35:16,134
command the floor like that,

750
00:35:16,636 --> 00:35:18,403
I couldn't help thinking,
"See? We knew what we were doing."

751
00:35:18,404 --> 00:35:20,505
"We trusted the right athletes."

752
00:35:21,474 --> 00:35:22,674
I was rooting for them the entire time.

753
00:35:23,042 --> 00:35:24,509
My eyes kept drifting right back
to their group.

754
00:35:24,510 --> 00:35:26,811
They really put on a show out there.

755
00:35:26,812 --> 00:35:30,248
A lot of the staff were blown away.

756
00:35:31,050 --> 00:35:32,517
(Meanwhile...)

757
00:35:33,286 --> 00:35:33,752
Ugh!

758
00:35:34,620 --> 00:35:36,187
- Good effort!
- Tough!

759
00:35:36,589 --> 00:35:39,491
(What position is enduring this gauntlet?)

760
00:35:40,560 --> 00:35:43,996
(Libero: the final defensive wall)

761
00:35:44,730 --> 00:35:47,966
(They throw their bodies on the line
to keep every rally alive.)

762
00:35:49,402 --> 00:35:52,004
The coaches are jumping on the boxes
to rip jump serves.

763
00:35:52,005 --> 00:35:53,271
(1. Digging heavy heat off
the coaches' platforms)

764
00:35:54,374 --> 00:35:56,875
The target is right here.
Drop it in the basket.

765
00:35:56,876 --> 00:35:57,676
(2. Pinpoint accuracy)

766
00:35:59,479 --> 00:36:00,478
We have to drop a pass inside that?

767
00:36:04,884 --> 00:36:06,418
(A rocket serve knocks her off balance.)

768
00:36:06,419 --> 00:36:08,453
It's been forever
since I faced that kind of velocity.

769
00:36:09,389 --> 00:36:10,622
This drill is no joke.

770
00:36:10,623 --> 00:36:12,157
(Difficulty: maximum)

771
00:36:14,727 --> 00:36:16,461
(A familiar face steps into the fire)

772
00:36:16,462 --> 00:36:17,963
(To be continued)

773
00:36:17,964 --> 00:36:20,298
(Wonder Dogs Season One libero:
Koo Hye In)

774
00:36:20,533 --> 00:36:21,433
Yes, Coach!

775
00:36:21,434 --> 00:36:22,934
(Her expression shifts completely!)

776
00:36:27,286 --> 00:36:30,088
(She tracks down the drop spot instantly.)

777
00:36:30,323 --> 00:36:31,156
Hit it!

778
00:36:32,124 --> 00:36:34,560
(Zeroing in...)

779
00:36:34,561 --> 00:36:36,194
(one throw at a time)

780
00:36:38,331 --> 00:36:39,632
(Koo Hye In: plus 1 for accuracy)

781
00:36:39,633 --> 00:36:40,732
Great ball!

782
00:36:41,501 --> 00:36:42,967
She looks way more composed
than last year.

783
00:36:44,370 --> 00:36:46,104
(Hye In shows the true caliber
of Season One.)

784
00:36:47,240 --> 00:36:49,475
(Chae Seon Ah: 15-year veteran pro)

785
00:36:54,213 --> 00:36:56,047
(Drops it clean in the cart
on her first attempt)

786
00:36:56,048 --> 00:36:58,049
(Hmm)

787
00:36:59,919 --> 00:37:00,752
Service!

788
00:37:02,021 --> 00:37:05,824
(The next ball clips the rim again.)

789
00:37:05,825 --> 00:37:06,825
Service!

790
00:37:07,293 --> 00:37:08,426
(Textbook dig)

791
00:37:10,630 --> 00:37:12,164
(Chae Seon Ah: plus 1 for accuracy)

792
00:37:12,165 --> 00:37:13,098
Hit it!

793
00:37:14,667 --> 00:37:16,501
Seon Ah really is in a tier of her own.

794
00:37:16,502 --> 00:37:19,904
Her score sheet is going to look pristine.

795
00:37:20,640 --> 00:37:24,009
She's already an elite player,
but she's dialed in even further today.

796
00:37:24,410 --> 00:37:25,210
Service!

797
00:37:27,180 --> 00:37:28,046
Service!

798
00:37:29,348 --> 00:37:30,281
She swallowed that up!
(Chae Seon Ah: plus 2 for accuracy)

799
00:37:31,116 --> 00:37:32,250
Let's work!

800
00:37:32,251 --> 00:37:33,184
(Nods)

801
00:37:33,953 --> 00:37:34,786
Pass!

802
00:37:35,388 --> 00:37:36,188
Hit it!

803
00:37:36,189 --> 00:37:37,656
(Refusing to back down)

804
00:37:39,611 --> 00:37:40,511
(Koo Hye In: plus 2 for accuracy)

805
00:37:42,299 --> 00:37:43,127
(Chae Seon Ah: plus 3 for accuracy)

806
00:37:44,475 --> 00:37:47,143
(Neck and neck in the standings)

807
00:37:47,144 --> 00:37:48,111
Huge!

808
00:37:48,412 --> 00:37:49,245
What a pass!

809
00:37:49,246 --> 00:37:51,912
(A fierce standoff between
two elite liberos)

810
00:38:00,505 --> 00:38:02,874
(Scores on the first try)

811
00:38:05,777 --> 00:38:07,012
(Seo Yu Kyung, Yangsan City)

812
00:38:10,048 --> 00:38:11,816
(Seo Yu Kyung: plus 1 point for accuracy)

813
00:38:12,173 --> 00:38:14,452
(Fiery)

814
00:38:17,455 --> 00:38:19,424
(Seo Yu Kyung: 2 points for accuracy)

815
00:38:22,360 --> 00:38:24,128
(Seo Yu Kyung: 3 points for accuracy)

816
00:38:26,364 --> 00:38:27,265
(Four points for accuracy)

817
00:38:27,499 --> 00:38:28,599
Great job, Yu Kyung.

818
00:38:35,073 --> 00:38:37,484
(Inspired by the praise,
she makes a diving dig.)

819
00:38:37,485 --> 00:38:39,644
I think Yu Kyung is pretty good.

820
00:38:40,723 --> 00:38:42,514
She doesn't make
any unnecessary movements.

821
00:38:43,841 --> 00:38:45,115
Yu Kyung is the best.

822
00:38:45,206 --> 00:38:47,499
She had an overwhelming number
of successful plays.

823
00:38:48,720 --> 00:38:51,323
(The First Generation of Wonder Dogs)

824
00:38:52,257 --> 00:38:54,860
(Fifteen years of professional experience)

825
00:38:55,827 --> 00:38:58,429
(An overwhelming newcomer)

826
00:39:00,265 --> 00:39:03,601
(Libero Showdown)

827
00:39:03,968 --> 00:39:07,105
(Meanwhile...)

828
00:39:19,884 --> 00:39:23,779
(Two other players were
locked in fierce competition.)

829
00:39:24,093 --> 00:39:25,866
I couldn't take my eyes off...

830
00:39:26,709 --> 00:39:29,895
Hyeon Ju from Pohang Sports Council.

831
00:39:31,162 --> 00:39:33,431
(They were on the same team
until last year.)

832
00:39:33,965 --> 00:39:37,435
(They both applied
for Season One tryouts.)

833
00:39:40,972 --> 00:39:45,410
(They competed in good faith.)

834
00:39:47,378 --> 00:39:50,682
(But only Young In made the cut.)

835
00:39:51,549 --> 00:39:54,252
(Afterward, Hyeon Ju transferred
to the Pohang City Sports Council.)

836
00:39:55,286 --> 00:39:59,624
(Securing the starting spiker position,)

837
00:40:01,159 --> 00:40:05,463
(and in endless competition with Young In)

838
00:40:06,931 --> 00:40:09,667
(The rival)

839
00:40:10,932 --> 00:40:12,070
Young In is my rival.

840
00:40:13,359 --> 00:40:15,172
I know her style inside and out.

841
00:40:16,190 --> 00:40:19,277
(Know your enemy, know yourself)

842
00:40:19,302 --> 00:40:20,578
I just want to win.

843
00:40:22,280 --> 00:40:25,650
(Opposite Spiker: the team's go-to player)

844
00:40:26,734 --> 00:40:30,888
(There's only one spot
for the opposite spiker in Season 2)

845
00:40:31,556 --> 00:40:34,225
(Only one person will make the cut.)

846
00:40:34,856 --> 00:40:36,753
(First up, Park Hyeon Ju)

847
00:40:36,777 --> 00:40:38,496
(Park Hyeon Ju: 1 point for attack)

848
00:40:40,531 --> 00:40:42,562
(Nodding)

849
00:40:42,827 --> 00:40:43,534
She's good.

850
00:40:47,042 --> 00:40:50,166
I'm the top opposite spiker.

851
00:40:55,791 --> 00:40:56,966
Okay, nice job.

852
00:40:58,449 --> 00:40:59,717
(Keeping a watchful eye)

853
00:41:01,109 --> 00:41:03,618
The more I play,
the more competitive I get.

854
00:41:03,651 --> 00:41:05,456
I'm really giving it my all.

855
00:41:06,591 --> 00:41:08,193
(Hyeon Ju spikes it even harder.)

856
00:41:09,260 --> 00:41:11,496
(Full power)

857
00:41:11,521 --> 00:41:13,030
(Out)

858
00:41:16,662 --> 00:41:17,969
I was nervous.

859
00:41:20,638 --> 00:41:22,006
(Hits the net)

860
00:41:22,707 --> 00:41:24,042
(Well...)

861
00:41:25,977 --> 00:41:28,012
(Hyeon Ju got past two blocks.)

862
00:41:29,480 --> 00:41:30,308
(Block)

863
00:41:31,816 --> 00:41:32,517
(Thud)

864
00:41:34,289 --> 00:41:36,189
It looks like Young In can't
see the block.

865
00:41:39,366 --> 00:41:41,233
Her performance was a bit disappointing,

866
00:41:41,733 --> 00:41:43,266
compared to last year.

867
00:41:45,530 --> 00:41:49,567
(As her anxiety grew,
she made mistake after mistake.)

868
00:41:53,715 --> 00:41:56,599
It was really tough.

869
00:41:56,685 --> 00:42:01,148
I do hope
the first-generation players get selected.

870
00:42:01,173 --> 00:42:04,015
I do hope they put on a good show, but...

871
00:42:05,280 --> 00:42:06,684
This is right.

872
00:42:06,709 --> 00:42:09,721
(In the previous position-specific tests,)

873
00:42:11,189 --> 00:42:15,026
(the first-generation players
showed great skill.)

874
00:42:15,133 --> 00:42:17,246
The Wonder Dogs are good.

875
00:42:17,270 --> 00:42:19,099
After all, they have
last year's experience.

876
00:42:19,897 --> 00:42:22,566
(It even looked like everyone might pass.)

877
00:42:23,101 --> 00:42:25,903
(But Young In's skills fall
just a bit short.)

878
00:42:26,404 --> 00:42:30,441
It seems like Young In didn't
really show her full potential.

879
00:42:31,499 --> 00:42:32,832
I might get cut.

880
00:42:32,833 --> 00:42:34,946
I was worried about that.

881
00:42:35,713 --> 00:42:39,383
(A crisis for the first generation)

882
00:42:39,835 --> 00:42:41,841
Bring it in, everyone.

883
00:42:43,633 --> 00:42:46,774
(Six-on-six practice game)

884
00:42:46,942 --> 00:42:49,385
In terms of game management,

885
00:42:49,410 --> 00:42:54,294
there are players
who can deliver at any moment.

886
00:42:54,319 --> 00:42:58,836
We're trying to select
players who excel at that.

887
00:42:59,461 --> 00:43:00,504
Movement,

888
00:43:01,829 --> 00:43:02,778
instincts,

889
00:43:03,472 --> 00:43:04,442
vision,

890
00:43:05,366 --> 00:43:06,210
and teamwork.

891
00:43:07,149 --> 00:43:08,818
We have to look at all of those things.

892
00:43:15,553 --> 00:43:19,466
How many first-generation players are
even here?

893
00:43:20,648 --> 00:43:22,026
(Enkhsoyol from Season One)

894
00:43:22,059 --> 00:43:24,295
(Back Chae Rim from Season One)

895
00:43:24,320 --> 00:43:26,797
(Koo Hye In from Season One)

896
00:43:26,822 --> 00:43:29,833
(Lee Jin from Season One)

897
00:43:33,571 --> 00:43:36,274
(Starting with Jin's serve)

898
00:43:41,766 --> 00:43:44,081
(Hye In's dig)

899
00:43:44,092 --> 00:43:46,350
(Jin's set)

900
00:43:46,375 --> 00:43:48,152
(Chae Rim's spike)

901
00:43:52,113 --> 00:43:53,190
Wow.

902
00:43:58,741 --> 00:43:59,835
Back C.

903
00:44:00,480 --> 00:44:02,800
- I'll cover the tips with you.
- Okay.

904
00:44:06,737 --> 00:44:08,772
(Back C, as planned)

905
00:44:09,974 --> 00:44:11,476
(Immediate quick cover)

906
00:44:12,810 --> 00:44:15,479
(Enkhsoyol attacks successfully.)

907
00:44:18,072 --> 00:44:20,451
Are you okay?

908
00:44:23,354 --> 00:44:26,357
(In the blink of an eye, it's 0 to 3.)

909
00:44:27,458 --> 00:44:29,527
(Smiling)

910
00:44:32,666 --> 00:44:35,754
Since they'd practiced together,

911
00:44:36,050 --> 00:44:38,741
I could tell their timing was spot-on.

912
00:44:39,839 --> 00:44:43,972
I'll go out there and give it my all too.

913
00:44:45,039 --> 00:44:47,778
I hope I get in soon,
before my body gets stiff.

914
00:44:48,713 --> 00:44:51,849
(Team switch)

915
00:44:52,783 --> 00:44:55,419
(Outside hitter Min Kyeong in)

916
00:44:55,566 --> 00:44:56,466
Hold on.

917
00:44:59,090 --> 00:45:02,326
(Checking the game stats)

918
00:45:09,000 --> 00:45:10,001
Cover!

919
00:45:11,873 --> 00:45:12,720
Cover!

920
00:45:14,839 --> 00:45:17,674
(A thunderous back attack)

921
00:45:18,807 --> 00:45:20,044
Nice set.

922
00:45:21,212 --> 00:45:23,147
(Interesting)

923
00:45:30,755 --> 00:45:32,423
(Sneaking up)

924
00:45:33,099 --> 00:45:38,663
(Approaching the court
as if spellbound by the battle cry)

925
00:45:42,204 --> 00:45:42,967
Slam it.

926
00:45:44,468 --> 00:45:48,333
(Ji Min Kyeong: 1 point for attack)

927
00:45:52,877 --> 00:45:55,613
(Ji Min Kyeong: 2 points
for her battle cry)

928
00:46:00,184 --> 00:46:03,487
(Ji Min Kyeong: 3 points for a block)

929
00:46:04,019 --> 00:46:06,123
She really stood out.

930
00:46:06,499 --> 00:46:08,133
(Before the 6-on-6 match)

931
00:46:08,158 --> 00:46:10,217
It's a shame about Min Kyeong.

932
00:46:10,599 --> 00:46:11,914
- Min Kyeong.
- I see.

933
00:46:11,939 --> 00:46:13,674
It'd be great if we picked
players like her.

934
00:46:13,699 --> 00:46:16,874
- But she's just not in good enough form.
- I know.

935
00:46:16,899 --> 00:46:18,733
Why is she out of form?

936
00:46:20,604 --> 00:46:23,974
(A player they watched
with lingering disappointment)

937
00:46:24,352 --> 00:46:25,159
The middle.

938
00:46:30,503 --> 00:46:31,949
I got it.

939
00:46:32,598 --> 00:46:35,453
(The eagle is summoned once again.)

940
00:46:41,259 --> 00:46:43,074
Can she adapt well?

941
00:46:43,099 --> 00:46:45,363
I wondered if she could move fast enough.

942
00:46:46,263 --> 00:46:47,529
(Diving)

943
00:46:47,554 --> 00:46:49,400
(Jumping)

944
00:46:54,999 --> 00:46:56,165
Nice job.

945
00:46:56,166 --> 00:46:57,566
- Well done.
- Well done.

946
00:46:58,045 --> 00:46:58,909
Nice set.

947
00:47:00,326 --> 00:47:02,913
This player looks promising.

948
00:47:09,104 --> 00:47:12,356
I was most concerned about Min Kyeong.

949
00:47:13,272 --> 00:47:16,378
She's been playing professionally
until this year.

950
00:47:18,028 --> 00:47:19,296
(Min Kyeong's attack)

951
00:47:20,030 --> 00:47:21,808
(Chae Rim's defense)

952
00:47:22,233 --> 00:47:23,734
(Min Kyeong's attack)

953
00:47:24,034 --> 00:47:26,236
(Chae Rim's defense)

954
00:47:28,139 --> 00:47:29,473
(Chae Rim's attack)

955
00:47:29,498 --> 00:47:31,642
(Min Kyeong's defense)

956
00:47:33,110 --> 00:47:36,847
(A heated outside hitter competition)

957
00:47:42,653 --> 00:47:44,622
(Chae Rim's attack fails.)

958
00:47:49,431 --> 00:47:52,366
Min Kyeong stood out.

959
00:47:52,933 --> 00:47:56,593
She reminded me a little of Seung Ju.

960
00:47:58,770 --> 00:48:02,112
(Enkhsoyol scores a point.)

961
00:48:02,907 --> 00:48:03,840
Hey, hit it!

962
00:48:03,841 --> 00:48:05,776
(Min Kyeong scores too!)

963
00:48:05,777 --> 00:48:06,710
My mistake.

964
00:48:07,912 --> 00:48:09,145
It's our chance!

965
00:48:09,480 --> 00:48:10,313
Stay sharp.

966
00:48:11,462 --> 00:48:13,163
(A 1-on-1 blocking situation)

967
00:48:15,126 --> 00:48:16,060
(Attack error)

968
00:48:16,061 --> 00:48:17,161
Goodness.

969
00:48:17,414 --> 00:48:18,914
(Sighing)

970
00:48:18,915 --> 00:48:21,450
Enkhsoyol, why would you hit it like that
against a single blocker?

971
00:48:21,451 --> 00:48:23,152
- That was a one-on-one chance.
- Right.

972
00:48:23,153 --> 00:48:24,420
"What should I do?"

973
00:48:24,822 --> 00:48:27,190
I got too competitive.

974
00:48:27,191 --> 00:48:29,559
(Her competitive streak leads
to an error.)

975
00:48:29,927 --> 00:48:31,895
Now that we've actually played a game,
you can really see the difference.

976
00:48:32,196 --> 00:48:34,063
Players who didn't stand out are starting
to catch my eye.

977
00:48:34,665 --> 00:48:36,566
Min Kyeong is much more proactive now,

978
00:48:36,567 --> 00:48:38,434
firing herself up and really going
after the ball.

979
00:48:38,435 --> 00:48:40,737
Weaknesses become
much more obvious in a real game.

980
00:48:41,622 --> 00:48:46,176
(The first-generation players are fired up
by the arrival of the new players.)

981
00:48:46,683 --> 00:48:47,510
(The Unpredictable 4)

982
00:48:47,511 --> 00:48:49,612
How does she know
how to score even without jumping?

983
00:48:49,980 --> 00:48:50,947
- Go ahead.
- Okay.

984
00:48:51,249 --> 00:48:52,782
- I'll get right to it.
- Yes, now.

985
00:48:53,884 --> 00:48:55,117
Please come in again.

986
00:48:55,118 --> 00:48:56,219
(While Yeon Koung is deep in thought...)

987
00:48:56,220 --> 00:48:57,153
Let's go!

988
00:48:58,189 --> 00:48:59,289
So I'm starting here now?

989
00:48:59,623 --> 00:49:01,691
This is your position, right?
Where are you starting?

990
00:49:01,692 --> 00:49:02,725
From Zone Six.

991
00:49:02,726 --> 00:49:03,993
Where did you finish last time?

992
00:49:03,994 --> 00:49:05,728
(Her voice catches
Yeon Koung's attention.)

993
00:49:06,263 --> 00:49:08,264
Wait. You, hold on a second!

994
00:49:08,999 --> 00:49:10,199
Why are you here?

995
00:49:11,603 --> 00:49:12,502
Here?

996
00:49:14,538 --> 00:49:15,905
Why are you here?

997
00:49:15,906 --> 00:49:16,772
(A stern look)

998
00:49:16,773 --> 00:49:19,442
At the start, I'm going
to push out from here like this...

999
00:49:19,443 --> 00:49:21,911
What? I told you to start
from where you finished last time.

1000
00:49:21,912 --> 00:49:24,180
- Got it.
- What is she even talking about?

1001
00:49:24,682 --> 00:49:25,448
(Pointing)
She still hasn't got it together.

1002
00:49:26,817 --> 00:49:27,817
I got scolded again.

1003
00:49:28,919 --> 00:49:29,986
I got scolded again.

1004
00:49:30,488 --> 00:49:33,557
(Reviewing the rules
for the 6-on-6 test match)

1005
00:49:33,558 --> 00:49:35,392
- Then you leave it here.
- Leave it here.

1006
00:49:36,060 --> 00:49:37,761
- Rotate!
- Time to rotate.

1007
00:49:38,795 --> 00:49:40,731
Where do you go next?

1008
00:49:40,732 --> 00:49:42,265
- Sorry?
- Where do you go after this?

1009
00:49:42,266 --> 00:49:43,300
What do you mean, Zone Three?

1010
00:49:43,301 --> 00:49:44,634
Where do you go after Zone One?

1011
00:49:44,635 --> 00:49:45,601
Zone Six.

1012
00:49:47,738 --> 00:49:49,238
Enkhsoyol got scolded again.

1013
00:49:50,241 --> 00:49:52,642
It's all because of you.
Because you took your position over there.

1014
00:49:52,643 --> 00:49:53,543
Sorry.

1015
00:49:54,178 --> 00:49:55,111
Darn it.

1016
00:49:57,948 --> 00:50:00,516
She's already in position.

1017
00:50:02,386 --> 00:50:05,355
She's still so clueless.
She's driving me crazy.

1018
00:50:10,094 --> 00:50:13,297
When Coach first explained the rules,
I honestly didn't understand her.

1019
00:50:13,298 --> 00:50:14,965
Right side or left side,
it doesn't matter.

1020
00:50:14,966 --> 00:50:17,567
The player in Zone 6 moves to 4,
and the player in 4 moves to 2.

1021
00:50:17,568 --> 00:50:18,935
- Got it?
- Yes.

1022
00:50:18,936 --> 00:50:20,670
- Did you all get it?
- Yes.

1023
00:50:20,671 --> 00:50:22,206
So I asked Song Hee later.

1024
00:50:22,207 --> 00:50:24,174
"What did Coach say earlier?"

1025
00:50:24,175 --> 00:50:25,609
And she explained it to me.

1026
00:50:25,610 --> 00:50:27,777
So I did exactly what she told me,

1027
00:50:27,778 --> 00:50:29,513
but she had it wrong too.

1028
00:50:29,514 --> 00:50:32,082
So I went up to her and said,
"Song Hee..."

1029
00:50:32,917 --> 00:50:34,717
Song Hee, you told me the wrong rule.

1030
00:50:34,718 --> 00:50:36,452
I know. That's why...

1031
00:50:36,453 --> 00:50:37,587
(Almost crying)

1032
00:50:37,588 --> 00:50:39,488
That's why Coach scolded me.

1033
00:50:39,924 --> 00:50:41,458
- It's okay.
- Sorry.

1034
00:50:41,859 --> 00:50:43,760
I thought, "If I get to be on Season Two,"

1035
00:50:44,061 --> 00:50:48,531
"I want to show a different side
of myself from Season One."

1036
00:50:48,532 --> 00:50:51,334
I didn't want to be like before,

1037
00:50:51,569 --> 00:50:54,704
just saying, "Yes, yes," when I didn't
really understand what was going on.

1038
00:50:54,705 --> 00:50:55,906
You know what I mean, right?

1039
00:50:55,907 --> 00:50:57,073
- Did you get it?
- Yes!

1040
00:50:57,074 --> 00:50:58,441
- You know what I mean, right?
- Yes!

1041
00:50:59,510 --> 00:51:00,610
Her answers are always so confident.

1042
00:51:01,579 --> 00:51:03,980
So I kept thinking,
"I can't be like this again."

1043
00:51:06,350 --> 00:51:08,484
(Sighing)

1044
00:51:09,186 --> 00:51:12,288
Enkhsoyol loses a few points
for being a bit clueless.

1045
00:51:12,823 --> 00:51:13,890
Because she's too clueless?

1046
00:51:13,891 --> 00:51:15,491
(Enkhsoyol: minus 1 for being clueless)

1047
00:51:15,627 --> 00:51:16,793
That silly girl.

1048
00:51:17,828 --> 00:51:20,396
She still hasn't learned after Season One.

1049
00:51:20,731 --> 00:51:22,699
She's still not there yet.

1050
00:51:23,367 --> 00:51:24,233
How were the setters?

1051
00:51:25,202 --> 00:51:26,269
How were they? Not bad?

1052
00:51:27,204 --> 00:51:28,671
They all have their strengths
and weaknesses.

1053
00:51:29,006 --> 00:51:30,373
Really? Who are you talking about?

1054
00:51:30,874 --> 00:51:32,174
Hyo Rim, Jin...

1055
00:51:33,544 --> 00:51:35,144
Who was the other one?
Da Sol. Those three.

1056
00:51:35,145 --> 00:51:36,179
Right.

1057
00:51:36,180 --> 00:51:37,747
I guess they're practicing on their own.

1058
00:51:37,748 --> 00:51:39,415
(Kim Da Sol, setter, released
from the Pink Spiders in 2026)

1059
00:51:40,583 --> 00:51:41,750
Please come in again.

1060
00:51:41,952 --> 00:51:42,885
Is it me?

1061
00:51:42,886 --> 00:51:45,488
(Setter Da Sol enters.)

1062
00:51:45,489 --> 00:51:46,355
Here we go.

1063
00:51:46,897 --> 00:51:49,265
If that doesn't work, I'll take
the right side. Let's cover defense here.

1064
00:51:52,869 --> 00:51:54,036
Let's go!

1065
00:51:55,205 --> 00:51:56,205
Here comes the chance.

1066
00:51:56,206 --> 00:51:57,506
(Da Sol)

1067
00:51:59,876 --> 00:52:01,091
- Mine!
- Get it!

1068
00:52:01,092 --> 00:52:01,958
(Blocker 1, Blocker 2)

1069
00:52:03,046 --> 00:52:04,613
Get it!

1070
00:52:04,614 --> 00:52:05,648
- That's it!
- Nice set.

1071
00:52:06,049 --> 00:52:07,049
Good.

1072
00:52:07,050 --> 00:52:08,450
(She sets toward the side
with fewer blockers.)

1073
00:52:08,451 --> 00:52:10,219
Keep going.

1074
00:52:13,323 --> 00:52:14,390
Hey!

1075
00:52:14,958 --> 00:52:16,425
(Blocker 1, Blocker 2)

1076
00:52:17,794 --> 00:52:18,727
Nice.

1077
00:52:18,728 --> 00:52:19,916
(She scores with ease.)

1078
00:52:19,917 --> 00:52:21,484
(Nice.)

1079
00:52:29,306 --> 00:52:30,306
Hit it!

1080
00:52:30,747 --> 00:52:32,075
(She completely fools the blockers.)

1081
00:52:32,209 --> 00:52:33,209
Hit it now.

1082
00:52:33,210 --> 00:52:35,043
Okay. Nice.

1083
00:52:36,380 --> 00:52:38,081
Da Sol, nice set.

1084
00:52:38,082 --> 00:52:39,349
(Veteran savvy)

1085
00:52:40,283 --> 00:52:41,116
That set...

1086
00:52:42,252 --> 00:52:44,686
She's good. That was a nice set.

1087
00:52:45,689 --> 00:52:47,957
Da Sol stands out, doesn't she?

1088
00:52:47,958 --> 00:52:49,458
- The control...
- She knows how to manage the game.

1089
00:52:49,459 --> 00:52:50,461
Definitely.

1090
00:52:50,462 --> 00:52:51,528
She knows how to send it deep,

1091
00:52:51,529 --> 00:52:52,662
and if they drop back, she keeps it short.

1092
00:52:52,663 --> 00:52:53,629
I think she's good.

1093
00:52:53,971 --> 00:52:54,997
She wasn't bad.

1094
00:52:56,500 --> 00:52:58,201
I wasn't nervous, but all of a sudden,

1095
00:52:58,702 --> 00:52:59,935
my heart started pounding.

1096
00:53:02,205 --> 00:53:03,372
Rotate.

1097
00:53:03,373 --> 00:53:06,809
(Jin enters.)

1098
00:53:07,611 --> 00:53:08,525
Nice.

1099
00:53:09,279 --> 00:53:10,179
Let's go!

1100
00:53:10,647 --> 00:53:13,082
(Game-Managing Setter Da Sol
vs. Power Setter Jin)

1101
00:53:15,419 --> 00:53:16,252
My ball.

1102
00:53:18,722 --> 00:53:19,989
- Nice.
- My ball!

1103
00:53:22,692 --> 00:53:23,558
Hit it!

1104
00:53:23,559 --> 00:53:24,860
(A powerful set)

1105
00:53:27,664 --> 00:53:28,764
Min Kyeong, nice!

1106
00:53:28,765 --> 00:53:30,132
- Go!
- Mine!

1107
00:53:31,601 --> 00:53:32,501
Now hit it.

1108
00:53:35,639 --> 00:53:37,306
(Da Sol fails to make the defensive play.)

1109
00:53:37,307 --> 00:53:38,207
(Panting)

1110
00:53:38,487 --> 00:53:39,287
My turn.

1111
00:53:39,403 --> 00:53:41,537
(Power Setter Jin scores.)

1112
00:53:41,538 --> 00:53:44,206
A lot of people have told me
that I have good power,

1113
00:53:44,207 --> 00:53:47,243
so when it came
to setting the second ball,

1114
00:53:47,244 --> 00:53:49,378
I think I was able to do it
with confidence.

1115
00:53:50,448 --> 00:53:52,716
(Exhaling)

1116
00:53:53,150 --> 00:53:54,718
(Exhaling)

1117
00:53:54,719 --> 00:53:58,788
I can't really compete with Jin
when it comes to pure power,

1118
00:53:58,789 --> 00:54:01,057
so I thought there was a chance
Jin might get picked again.

1119
00:54:02,961 --> 00:54:07,197
But I do think
I'm a little better defensively.

1120
00:54:07,198 --> 00:54:08,031
(Chuckling)

1121
00:54:09,734 --> 00:54:10,634
(Jin fails at defense.)
Sorry.

1122
00:54:11,802 --> 00:54:12,635
It's a chance!

1123
00:54:13,771 --> 00:54:14,871
Hey, Young In!

1124
00:54:17,942 --> 00:54:19,542
(Da Sol with a spectacular dig!)

1125
00:54:19,543 --> 00:54:21,111
(Nodding)

1126
00:54:23,814 --> 00:54:25,782
(Kim Da Sol: plus 1 for defense)

1127
00:54:25,783 --> 00:54:26,816
Nice defense.

1128
00:54:27,518 --> 00:54:28,318
Work together.

1129
00:54:29,787 --> 00:54:32,622
I could feel myself getting
into better form.

1130
00:54:33,892 --> 00:54:36,927
Keeping the ball alive on defense
and turning it into an attack,

1131
00:54:36,928 --> 00:54:38,094
Her defense was good earlier.

1132
00:54:38,430 --> 00:54:41,798
or making better underhand sets
on low balls...

1133
00:54:41,799 --> 00:54:42,699
Get it!

1134
00:54:44,402 --> 00:54:46,176
(Kim Da Sol: plus 1 for underhand setting)

1135
00:54:46,804 --> 00:54:48,238
(Sighing)

1136
00:54:48,940 --> 00:54:51,574
For things like that,
I felt more confident.

1137
00:54:51,575 --> 00:54:52,943
(Kim Da Sol: plus 1 for a quick attack)

1138
00:54:55,379 --> 00:54:56,813
(Even calmly pulling off a pass feint)

1139
00:54:56,814 --> 00:54:58,748
Well done, everyone.

1140
00:54:58,850 --> 00:55:01,084
If I really play to my strengths
in those areas,

1141
00:55:01,152 --> 00:55:02,319
I might have a chance to get selected.

1142
00:55:02,320 --> 00:55:03,620
Da Sol seems like the best one so far.

1143
00:55:03,621 --> 00:55:05,622
She's the best right now.

1144
00:55:05,990 --> 00:55:08,625
Right now, we can't run the game
without Da Sol.

1145
00:55:10,327 --> 00:55:11,294
(Sighing)

1146
00:55:11,296 --> 00:55:13,629
I think I just couldn't stay focused
at that point.

1147
00:55:14,865 --> 00:55:16,799
(Jin starts to get nervous.)

1148
00:55:17,568 --> 00:55:19,636
(Hyo Rim, standing beside her,
starts getting nervous too.)

1149
00:55:19,637 --> 00:55:23,339
I didn't realize Da Sol was that good.

1150
00:55:24,375 --> 00:55:27,443
Hello, I'm Ha Hyo Rim, a setter...

1151
00:55:27,444 --> 00:55:29,946
for the Suwon Special City
volleyball team.

1152
00:55:30,514 --> 00:55:32,415
(The Suwon Special City setter
who gave...)

1153
00:55:32,783 --> 00:55:35,418
(the Wonder Dogs trouble last season)

1154
00:55:36,720 --> 00:55:41,090
(The very player
who shook Jin's confidence)

1155
00:55:43,594 --> 00:55:48,131
(The rivals meet again
at the tryout one year later.)

1156
00:55:49,233 --> 00:55:50,066
Hey!

1157
00:55:50,067 --> 00:55:51,701
(During the accuracy test)

1158
00:55:52,937 --> 00:55:53,803
Yes.
(Perfect placement)

1159
00:55:57,007 --> 00:55:57,940
(Another perfect placement)

1160
00:55:59,710 --> 00:56:01,545
(Another perfect shot into the basket)

1161
00:56:01,546 --> 00:56:02,478
- Nice.
- Good.
Nice.

1162
00:56:04,882 --> 00:56:06,950
(The back set is right on target too.)

1163
00:56:07,052 --> 00:56:10,053
- She is definitely the most consistent.
- Hyo Rim is...

1164
00:56:10,054 --> 00:56:10,987
She's so...

1165
00:56:11,355 --> 00:56:12,855
Hyo Rim is really good.

1166
00:56:12,923 --> 00:56:14,223
She's way too good.

1167
00:56:15,593 --> 00:56:18,328
(Hyo Rim, the steady setter)

1168
00:56:18,329 --> 00:56:19,296
Catch it.

1169
00:56:20,364 --> 00:56:23,066
(Now her competition is
the rapidly rising Da Sol.)

1170
00:56:23,300 --> 00:56:25,001
(Game-Managing Setter Da Sol
vs. Steady Setter Hyo Rim)

1171
00:56:25,002 --> 00:56:25,801
Ready.

1172
00:56:26,004 --> 00:56:27,170
Dribble.

1173
00:56:28,205 --> 00:56:29,739
Again! You can pass too.

1174
00:56:30,608 --> 00:56:31,508
Hit it!
Nice.

1175
00:56:33,578 --> 00:56:35,145
(Hyo Rim makes the dig with ease.)

1176
00:56:35,913 --> 00:56:36,746
Nice! A chance!

1177
00:56:37,047 --> 00:56:38,347
Hit it! Now!

1178
00:56:38,348 --> 00:56:39,348
Hit it!

1179
00:56:40,151 --> 00:56:41,651
Good job.

1180
00:56:41,652 --> 00:56:43,220
(Da Sol keeps the pressure on.)

1181
00:56:43,420 --> 00:56:44,353
(Peeking)

1182
00:56:46,190 --> 00:56:49,024
I wanted to try everything,
whether it worked or not.

1183
00:56:49,025 --> 00:56:51,827
I thought, "Let's go for it. Let's do it.
You have to win no matter what."

1184
00:56:54,498 --> 00:56:56,800
Enkhsoyol, want a set on the right?

1185
00:56:56,801 --> 00:56:58,101
- Yes, please.
- Okay.

1186
00:56:59,003 --> 00:57:00,136
- Get to your position!
- Let's go.

1187
00:57:03,874 --> 00:57:06,642
(Input: Enkhsoyol sets the ball.)

1188
00:57:07,244 --> 00:57:08,110
Go!

1189
00:57:08,512 --> 00:57:09,779
(Output)

1190
00:57:09,780 --> 00:57:11,848
Nice!

1191
00:57:11,849 --> 00:57:12,949
Hurry up!

1192
00:57:13,150 --> 00:57:14,117
That's it!

1193
00:57:14,318 --> 00:57:15,217
No!

1194
00:57:18,255 --> 00:57:19,755
To the middle. Song Hee.

1195
00:57:20,058 --> 00:57:21,057
Pipe.

1196
00:57:22,293 --> 00:57:23,860
- More.
- To the middle.

1197
00:57:23,861 --> 00:57:25,095
(Song Hee goes
for a middle back-row attack.)

1198
00:57:25,096 --> 00:57:26,896
Hey!

1199
00:57:26,897 --> 00:57:27,798
(Output)

1200
00:57:27,823 --> 00:57:29,823
Nice! Good.

1201
00:57:30,534 --> 00:57:31,701
You did your best.

1202
00:57:31,702 --> 00:57:34,070
Doesn't Hyo Rim look like she has
complete control of the ball?

1203
00:57:34,605 --> 00:57:35,471
Absolutely.

1204
00:57:35,773 --> 00:57:36,706
It's up!

1205
00:57:37,142 --> 00:57:38,408
Put it away!

1206
00:57:38,409 --> 00:57:39,576
One more!

1207
00:57:39,910 --> 00:57:40,910
Two blockers!

1208
00:57:41,478 --> 00:57:43,099
(Her play leads directly to a point.)

1209
00:57:45,235 --> 00:57:46,268
Hit it!

1210
00:57:46,282 --> 00:57:47,130
That's it.

1211
00:57:47,131 --> 00:57:48,131
Hit it!

1212
00:57:49,719 --> 00:57:51,018
(Led successfully)

1213
00:57:51,019 --> 00:57:52,286
- All right, nice!
- Nice!

1214
00:57:53,819 --> 00:57:55,319
(Sighing)

1215
00:57:55,453 --> 00:57:56,919
She's a great setter.

1216
00:57:57,853 --> 00:58:00,253
What a massive showdown
between the setters.

1217
00:58:00,453 --> 00:58:01,817
They're completely different
in an actual game.

1218
00:58:02,219 --> 00:58:03,619
They all play differently.

1219
00:58:05,719 --> 00:58:07,286
Hyo Rim is doing splendidly.

1220
00:58:07,586 --> 00:58:10,719
- She's good enough to go pro.
- You're right.

1221
00:58:13,119 --> 00:58:15,052
They'll fall apart without Da Sol.

1222
00:58:15,053 --> 00:58:16,318
She's actually good!

1223
00:58:16,319 --> 00:58:17,753
She might make it.

1224
00:58:18,986 --> 00:58:21,185
(To claim the victory,)

1225
00:58:21,186 --> 00:58:23,086
(she even takes off her name tag.)

1226
00:58:23,353 --> 00:58:24,485
- Mine!
- Hit it again!

1227
00:58:24,486 --> 00:58:26,218
Jin's high balls are no joke.

1228
00:58:26,219 --> 00:58:27,618
Yes, just like before.

1229
00:58:27,619 --> 00:58:28,686
(Unmatched power)

1230
00:58:29,553 --> 00:58:31,686
(An ultimate battle
between three different setters)

1231
00:58:32,319 --> 00:58:34,686
(Who will be the setter
for the Wonder Dogs?)

1232
00:58:35,319 --> 00:58:36,352
In 1, 2.

1233
00:58:36,353 --> 00:58:37,353
Hit it!

1234
00:58:49,153 --> 00:58:51,186
I'm even more desperate
and want to do better.

1235
00:58:51,486 --> 00:58:54,853
As someone from last season,
I felt a lot of pressure,

1236
00:58:55,219 --> 00:58:57,785
and I believed it was up to me
to overcome it.

1237
00:58:57,786 --> 00:58:59,486
I thought I should go for it...

1238
00:58:59,786 --> 00:59:00,786
with confidence.

1239
00:59:04,053 --> 00:59:06,885
(Once again,)

1240
00:59:06,886 --> 00:59:09,653
(she faces her rival.)

1241
00:59:10,419 --> 00:59:11,452
In 1, 2!

1242
00:59:11,453 --> 00:59:14,319
(Hyeon Ju attacks.)

1243
00:59:15,619 --> 00:59:16,619
Hit it!

1244
00:59:17,386 --> 00:59:19,919
(Young In attacks next.)

1245
00:59:20,953 --> 00:59:21,985
Hit it!

1246
00:59:21,986 --> 00:59:23,752
(Another spike from Hyeon Ju)

1247
00:59:23,753 --> 00:59:26,219
(Hyeon Ju scores.)

1248
00:59:28,753 --> 00:59:29,853
I want to win.

1249
00:59:30,353 --> 00:59:33,786
I didn't want to bring shame
to my Wonder Dogs jersey.

1250
00:59:34,153 --> 00:59:36,753
Nice ball! Hyeon Ju, right back!

1251
00:59:37,319 --> 00:59:38,785
(Hyeon Ju attacks.)

1252
00:59:38,786 --> 00:59:40,418
(Young In digs.)

1253
00:59:40,419 --> 00:59:41,585
Free ball!

1254
00:59:41,586 --> 00:59:42,586
Young In, give it now!

1255
00:59:42,719 --> 00:59:43,719
(Young In attacks.)

1256
00:59:43,720 --> 00:59:45,153
(Hyeon Ju digs.)

1257
00:59:45,353 --> 00:59:46,353
Go!

1258
00:59:46,486 --> 00:59:48,085
(This time,)

1259
00:59:48,086 --> 00:59:50,353
(I'm breaking through!)

1260
00:59:51,886 --> 00:59:53,786
(Young In scores.)

1261
00:59:58,186 --> 00:59:59,386
(Getting up)

1262
00:59:59,753 --> 01:00:00,753
Sorry, Hyeon Ju.

1263
01:00:02,019 --> 01:00:03,019
The middle!

1264
01:00:04,386 --> 01:00:06,253
(Troubled)

1265
01:00:06,753 --> 01:00:08,019
I think I can take her.

1266
01:00:11,019 --> 01:00:12,086
Hit it! They're one down!

1267
01:00:13,386 --> 01:00:17,386
(Young In's back-to-back points)

1268
01:00:19,653 --> 01:00:21,085
(Flustered)

1269
01:00:21,086 --> 01:00:22,119
Nice ball!

1270
01:00:25,053 --> 01:00:27,419
(After shaking off her sluggishness,)

1271
01:00:28,353 --> 01:00:30,585
(Young In bounces back.)

1272
01:00:30,586 --> 01:00:33,386
You just need to hit it that way.

1273
01:00:33,753 --> 01:00:34,819
Great spike.

1274
01:00:36,353 --> 01:00:37,452
Young In?

1275
01:00:37,453 --> 01:00:38,686
I want to beat her.

1276
01:00:40,119 --> 01:00:41,753
- Hyeon Ju!
- Go!

1277
01:00:44,019 --> 01:00:45,953
(Hyeon Ju spikes.)

1278
01:00:46,419 --> 01:00:49,318
(Young In blocks.)

1279
01:00:49,319 --> 01:00:50,719
Free ball!

1280
01:00:52,053 --> 01:00:53,053
She's good.

1281
01:00:54,086 --> 01:00:55,119
This is driving me crazy.

1282
01:00:55,919 --> 01:00:57,353
We've got some fine players here.

1283
01:00:58,686 --> 01:00:59,986
They're all scary.

1284
01:01:00,386 --> 01:01:02,085
Everyone is doing great.

1285
01:01:02,086 --> 01:01:04,118
There are many amazing players.

1286
01:01:04,119 --> 01:01:05,519
Some of them are pretty decent.

1287
01:01:06,386 --> 01:01:07,785
It's so hard to choose.

1288
01:01:07,786 --> 01:01:11,019
(Who will be the new faces
of the Wonder Dogs?)

1289
01:01:13,386 --> 01:01:18,686
(The Wonder Dogs' team launch day)

1290
01:01:19,153 --> 01:01:21,386
(Elegant structures are lined...)

1291
01:01:21,619 --> 01:01:23,953
(with a sea of welcome banners.)

1292
01:01:25,186 --> 01:01:30,253
(The first recruit makes
a confident entrance.)

1293
01:01:31,153 --> 01:01:32,153
Wow.

1294
01:01:33,886 --> 01:01:36,053
We're having a ceremony here too.

1295
01:01:48,553 --> 01:01:54,319
(Enkhsoyol, 180cm,
Mokpo Science University)

1296
01:01:55,086 --> 01:01:56,185
Hello.

1297
01:01:56,186 --> 01:01:58,853
I'm Enkhsoyol from Mongolia.

1298
01:01:59,353 --> 01:02:03,052
(Her Korean has improved.)

1299
01:02:03,053 --> 01:02:04,053
Yes.

1300
01:02:05,653 --> 01:02:06,719
Enkhsoyol...

1301
01:02:07,419 --> 01:02:09,753
was chosen first.

1302
01:02:12,186 --> 01:02:13,653
(Smacking)

1303
01:02:14,386 --> 01:02:16,518
(Powerful attacks...)

1304
01:02:16,519 --> 01:02:18,652
Her strength lies in her attacks.

1305
01:02:18,653 --> 01:02:19,752
(that break through blocks.)

1306
01:02:19,753 --> 01:02:21,019
She might sprain her finger.

1307
01:02:21,519 --> 01:02:22,553
Gosh.

1308
01:02:27,186 --> 01:02:28,218
It's 297cm.

1309
01:02:28,219 --> 01:02:30,085
(First in running jump)

1310
01:02:30,086 --> 01:02:33,218
Enkhsoyol loses a point
for being a little clumsy.

1311
01:02:33,219 --> 01:02:34,953
(Overwhelming attack skills...)

1312
01:02:35,553 --> 01:02:37,486
She showcased a lot of her strengths,

1313
01:02:37,786 --> 01:02:39,885
surprising all the coaching staff.

1314
01:02:39,886 --> 01:02:41,186
(that outweigh her clumsiness)

1315
01:02:42,019 --> 01:02:45,653
(Enkhsoyol, their top pick)

1316
01:02:45,953 --> 01:02:51,219
Last year, I wasn't able
to show everything I had.

1317
01:02:52,319 --> 01:02:56,118
I felt like I needed to take
more responsibility...

1318
01:02:56,119 --> 01:02:58,653
and work harder this time.

1319
01:03:02,753 --> 01:03:03,819
(Pondering)

1320
01:03:07,019 --> 01:03:09,553
(Looking around)

1321
01:03:10,186 --> 01:03:12,186
When I first saw the venue,

1322
01:03:14,353 --> 01:03:17,319
I could see they've upgraded things
for the second season.

1323
01:03:18,186 --> 01:03:21,453
It looked much better
than the first season.

1324
01:03:22,786 --> 01:03:26,786
I was even more excited
for the new season.

1325
01:03:28,453 --> 01:03:32,086
(Another outside hitter to join the team)

1326
01:03:38,053 --> 01:03:39,253
Oh, hey!

1327
01:03:41,653 --> 01:03:46,319
(Back Chae Rim, 173cm, Suwon Special City)

1328
01:03:46,986 --> 01:03:48,053
- Hello.
- Hello.

1329
01:03:48,853 --> 01:03:49,886
Hi!

1330
01:03:52,453 --> 01:03:54,119
- Let's give it our best again.
- Okay.

1331
01:03:55,153 --> 01:03:56,785
As for Chae Rim,

1332
01:03:56,786 --> 01:03:59,619
she's the most well-balanced
in both attack and defense.

1333
01:04:00,486 --> 01:04:02,485
Back in the first season,

1334
01:04:02,486 --> 01:04:05,918
I was told I was chosen
for my defensive skills.

1335
01:04:05,919 --> 01:04:07,353
(A solid defense)

1336
01:04:07,919 --> 01:04:09,818
But I think my attacking has improved.

1337
01:04:09,819 --> 01:04:12,353
(An all-rounder
who's excellent on offense too)

1338
01:04:13,386 --> 01:04:16,152
If we have Chae Rim on the team,

1339
01:04:16,153 --> 01:04:19,119
she'd be able to fulfill so many roles.

1340
01:04:19,553 --> 01:04:21,252
She looked reliable.

1341
01:04:21,253 --> 01:04:22,519
(The team's backbone)

1342
01:04:23,053 --> 01:04:25,285
- Last year, it was a founding ceremony.
- Right.

1343
01:04:25,286 --> 01:04:27,852
- It's a launch ceremony this year.
- A launch ceremony.

1344
01:04:27,853 --> 01:04:30,919
- Things have gotten a lot bigger.
- I know.

1345
01:04:36,353 --> 01:04:37,453
Someone's coming.

1346
01:04:39,219 --> 01:04:43,019
(The third outsider hitter to advance)

1347
01:04:43,519 --> 01:04:45,653
- Hi.
- It's Song Hee.

1348
01:04:46,919 --> 01:04:49,053
(Happy to see her)

1349
01:04:49,553 --> 01:04:52,019
- Congratulations, Song Hee.
- Congratulations.

1350
01:04:52,753 --> 01:04:53,986
Hi, Enkhsoyol.

1351
01:04:55,353 --> 01:04:57,652
I was absolutely stunned.

1352
01:04:57,653 --> 01:05:01,153
Song Hee seems to be
in much better shape now.

1353
01:05:02,219 --> 01:05:03,253
(Shouting)

1354
01:05:04,353 --> 01:05:05,353
(Shouting)

1355
01:05:07,253 --> 01:05:08,786
She can hit that hard?

1356
01:05:10,386 --> 01:05:12,418
Song Hee is built really well.

1357
01:05:12,419 --> 01:05:13,553
Her attacks are just...

1358
01:05:13,886 --> 01:05:15,053
Wow, Song Hee.

1359
01:05:16,153 --> 01:05:18,152
Few outsider hitters can attack
from the right.

1360
01:05:18,153 --> 01:05:20,153
Song Hee is pretty great
at right-side attacks too.

1361
01:05:23,886 --> 01:05:26,953
(A little giant...)

1362
01:05:28,286 --> 01:05:30,718
I loved her energy.

1363
01:05:30,719 --> 01:05:32,352
(who fearlessly soars high)

1364
01:05:32,353 --> 01:05:35,819
(The little giant is back.)

1365
01:05:36,153 --> 01:05:39,153
We have higher hopes for her
in this second season.

1366
01:05:40,386 --> 01:05:44,886
So far, only players
from the first season have made it.

1367
01:05:45,719 --> 01:05:47,919
(Among the first-season players,)

1368
01:05:48,753 --> 01:05:51,952
(three have made the cut.)

1369
01:05:51,953 --> 01:05:53,486
So the next one might be...

1370
01:05:54,219 --> 01:05:58,553
someone from the last season too.

1371
01:05:59,219 --> 01:06:00,353
I wonder who it'll be.

1372
01:06:03,253 --> 01:06:08,086
(Is it a first-season player
as Chae Rim expected?)

1373
01:06:16,253 --> 01:06:18,052
- Hello, Min Kyeong.
- Hello.

1374
01:06:18,053 --> 01:06:20,618
(Ji Min Kyeong, 183cm, unaffiliated)

1375
01:06:20,619 --> 01:06:21,619
Congratulations, Min Kyeong.

1376
01:06:21,620 --> 01:06:23,186
- Congratulations.
- Congratulations, Min Kyeong.

1377
01:06:25,853 --> 01:06:31,653
I liked how desperate Min Kyeong was.

1378
01:06:32,353 --> 01:06:35,185
(Even though she falls over...)

1379
01:06:35,186 --> 01:06:36,453
(and over,)

1380
01:06:36,619 --> 01:06:37,619
One more!

1381
01:06:38,286 --> 01:06:39,785
(One more!)

1382
01:06:39,786 --> 01:06:41,486
I could tell from her face
how serious she was.

1383
01:06:41,986 --> 01:06:43,453
I could see how badly she wanted it.

1384
01:06:44,853 --> 01:06:48,318
But we couldn't recruit her
based on emotions alone.

1385
01:06:48,319 --> 01:06:50,686
Her skill had to come first.

1386
01:06:51,686 --> 01:06:53,186
(Good right-side attacks)

1387
01:06:53,486 --> 01:06:54,719
(Good left-side attacks)

1388
01:06:55,186 --> 01:06:56,853
(Even a middle back-row attack)

1389
01:06:57,786 --> 01:06:59,052
(Skills beyond desperation)

1390
01:06:59,053 --> 01:07:00,953
She might be a great fit.

1391
01:07:01,486 --> 01:07:02,785
- Is Min Kyeong better?
- Much better.

1392
01:07:02,786 --> 01:07:04,253
- Min Kyeong.
- She's pretty good.

1393
01:07:04,486 --> 01:07:08,319
(The rookie coach's definite pick)

1394
01:07:08,786 --> 01:07:12,186
We're playing together again
like at Sunmyung Girls High School.

1395
01:07:12,486 --> 01:07:13,885
- It's been so long.
- Exactly.

1396
01:07:13,886 --> 01:07:15,186
(They went to the same high school.)

1397
01:07:15,453 --> 01:07:16,453
I can't wait.

1398
01:07:16,953 --> 01:07:18,086
- Let's have fun.
- Sure.

1399
01:07:20,219 --> 01:07:22,853
(The first setter to advance)

1400
01:07:37,253 --> 01:07:39,118
- Hello.
- Hello.

1401
01:07:39,119 --> 01:07:40,519
(Kim Da Sol, 173cm, unaffiliated)

1402
01:07:40,793 --> 01:07:42,919
- Hello.
- Hello.

1403
01:07:43,553 --> 01:07:44,553
She's so pretty.

1404
01:07:46,482 --> 01:07:47,649
- Hi.
- You made it.

1405
01:07:49,051 --> 01:07:49,884
The setters.

1406
01:07:50,486 --> 01:07:53,088
If I had to pick just one,

1407
01:07:53,489 --> 01:07:56,624
I'd pick Kim Da Sol.
She's definitely my first choice.

1408
01:07:56,892 --> 01:07:58,192
- Same here.
- Me too.

1409
01:07:58,193 --> 01:07:59,160
I agree.

1410
01:07:59,161 --> 01:08:00,495
We all agree too.

1411
01:08:00,496 --> 01:08:01,462
- Everyone agrees?
- Yes.

1412
01:08:01,463 --> 01:08:02,697
(Unanimous decision)

1413
01:08:02,698 --> 01:08:03,965
Right.

1414
01:08:03,966 --> 01:08:05,533
We know exactly what Da Sol can offer.

1415
01:08:06,268 --> 01:08:07,602
Her speed.

1416
01:08:07,603 --> 01:08:09,136
(From lightning-fast quick attacks...)

1417
01:08:09,137 --> 01:08:10,871
She makes the most of a perfect pass.

1418
01:08:11,073 --> 01:08:13,141
(to sets for slide attacks...)

1419
01:08:13,408 --> 01:08:14,742
Her game management is solid.

1420
01:08:15,177 --> 01:08:17,412
(and smart game management)

1421
01:08:17,513 --> 01:08:20,415
(We've found our top pick.)

1422
01:08:20,416 --> 01:08:21,516
(Watching intently)

1423
01:08:21,517 --> 01:08:24,719
She was every coach's first choice,

1424
01:08:24,720 --> 01:08:25,854
so she made the team.

1425
01:08:25,855 --> 01:08:26,888
(Kim Da Sol, the coaches' top pick)

1426
01:08:27,890 --> 01:08:30,825
(Next up, the middle blockers)

1427
01:08:36,365 --> 01:08:37,265
Who is that?

1428
01:08:38,667 --> 01:08:40,968
- It's Ho Bin!
- Let's go!

1429
01:08:40,969 --> 01:08:43,237
(Lee Ho Bin, 182cm, Pohang Sports Council)

1430
01:08:44,473 --> 01:08:45,541
It's Ye Dam!

1431
01:08:45,542 --> 01:08:47,175
(Lee Ye Dam, 185cm,
Suwon Special City Hall)

1432
01:08:47,743 --> 01:08:49,043
- Bo Been!
- Hello.

1433
01:08:49,044 --> 01:08:52,046
(Kim Bo Been, 180cm,
Suwon Special City Hall)

1434
01:08:52,347 --> 01:08:53,547
The middles!

1435
01:08:54,016 --> 01:08:56,351
I think all the middle blockers are
here now, right?

1436
01:08:56,352 --> 01:08:57,952
(The Season 2 middle blocker trio)

1437
01:08:58,221 --> 01:08:59,687
As for Bo Been,

1438
01:09:00,722 --> 01:09:03,723
she's really good at slide attacks,

1439
01:09:03,724 --> 01:09:04,825
which is a big strength of hers.

1440
01:09:04,826 --> 01:09:07,161
(Middle blocker Kim Bo Been)

1441
01:09:07,162 --> 01:09:08,529
And Ho Bin is...

1442
01:09:08,897 --> 01:09:11,966
really good at quick attacks
in front of the setter.

1443
01:09:11,967 --> 01:09:14,168
(She excels at sharp, quick attacks.)

1444
01:09:14,803 --> 01:09:15,803
Okay!

1445
01:09:15,804 --> 01:09:17,605
(Middle blocker Lee Ho Bin)

1446
01:09:17,606 --> 01:09:19,440
As for Ye Dam,

1447
01:09:19,441 --> 01:09:22,743
I think she's a good all-around player.

1448
01:09:25,180 --> 01:09:26,046
Hit it!

1449
01:09:26,815 --> 01:09:28,349
Her blocking was good.

1450
01:09:28,350 --> 01:09:30,151
(From her height...)

1451
01:09:30,152 --> 01:09:31,053
(to her attacks)

1452
01:09:31,054 --> 01:09:32,453
She was good on offense too.

1453
01:09:32,454 --> 01:09:33,287
Nice!

1454
01:09:33,288 --> 01:09:35,756
She's been the most impressive
of the middle blockers.

1455
01:09:35,757 --> 01:09:36,957
(Middle blocker Lee Ye Dam)

1456
01:09:36,958 --> 01:09:40,560
Compared to last year,
we have middle blockers...

1457
01:09:40,561 --> 01:09:42,696
who can contribute more on offense,

1458
01:09:43,265 --> 01:09:45,466
so I think they'll work well together.

1459
01:09:57,046 --> 01:10:00,314
(Seo Yu Kyung, 167cm, Yangsan City Hall)

1460
01:10:00,782 --> 01:10:01,615
Seo Yu Kyung.
(Happy to see her)

1461
01:10:03,785 --> 01:10:05,486
- Congrats, Yu Kyung.
- Thank you.

1462
01:10:06,589 --> 01:10:08,989
How did the liberos do? Who stood out?

1463
01:10:08,990 --> 01:10:10,924
- Seo Yu Kyung.
- Yu Kyung.

1464
01:10:10,925 --> 01:10:11,925
Seo Yu Kyung for me too.

1465
01:10:11,926 --> 01:10:13,794
- Seo Yu Kyung?
- She handles deep balls well.

1466
01:10:14,196 --> 01:10:14,996
Mine!

1467
01:10:15,430 --> 01:10:16,397
That's it.
(On target from deep)

1468
01:10:17,199 --> 01:10:18,565
She handles short balls well too.

1469
01:10:18,566 --> 01:10:19,700
Mine!

1470
01:10:19,701 --> 01:10:20,901
(On target from close range)

1471
01:10:21,203 --> 01:10:22,437
(Every pass...)

1472
01:10:22,438 --> 01:10:25,373
(lands right in the basket.)

1473
01:10:25,640 --> 01:10:26,807
(Even in matches,)

1474
01:10:26,808 --> 01:10:27,741
Mine!

1475
01:10:27,742 --> 01:10:29,576
(she excels at receiving...)

1476
01:10:30,212 --> 01:10:31,612
(and defense.)

1477
01:10:32,581 --> 01:10:34,749
Yu Kyung had the highest accuracy.

1478
01:10:34,750 --> 01:10:35,984
She was way ahead of the others.

1479
01:10:35,985 --> 01:10:37,985
Right. She's good.
She doesn't waste a single movement.

1480
01:10:39,321 --> 01:10:40,388
Okay!

1481
01:10:41,523 --> 01:10:42,189
(Thumbs up!)

1482
01:10:42,190 --> 01:10:43,257
Looking good, Yu Kyung!

1483
01:10:43,959 --> 01:10:45,760
(Yay!)

1484
01:10:46,128 --> 01:10:49,464
I think we've found a hidden gem.

1485
01:10:49,465 --> 01:10:50,399
(A hidden gem of a libero)

1486
01:10:51,400 --> 01:10:52,467
Who do you think will show up next?

1487
01:10:54,703 --> 01:10:56,137
I keep looking at the door.

1488
01:11:10,419 --> 01:11:11,719
(What?)

1489
01:11:14,756 --> 01:11:16,090
Oh, it's Ye Eun.

1490
01:11:16,558 --> 01:11:18,058
Hi.

1491
01:11:22,197 --> 01:11:23,764
- Oh, Ye Eun!
- Yes?

1492
01:11:23,765 --> 01:11:25,366
- Hi.
- Hello.

1493
01:11:25,367 --> 01:11:26,367
What are you doing here?

1494
01:11:26,869 --> 01:11:29,470
I wasn't expecting her to show up,

1495
01:11:30,005 --> 01:11:31,271
so I was really surprised.

1496
01:11:32,240 --> 01:11:35,375
I wondered why she was here
instead of playing in the pro league.

1497
01:11:36,111 --> 01:11:39,147
I arrived just last night...

1498
01:11:39,148 --> 01:11:40,648
and did the tryout on my own.

1499
01:11:42,952 --> 01:11:45,153
Could we get a roll of gimbap each too?

1500
01:11:45,355 --> 01:11:46,487
We're running short.

1501
01:11:46,888 --> 01:11:48,121
Thank you.

1502
01:11:48,122 --> 01:11:50,526
(Staring)

1503
01:11:50,527 --> 01:11:52,192
Oh, it's spam today.

1504
01:11:52,294 --> 01:11:53,928
- I heard Ye Eun asked to leave her team.
- What?

1505
01:11:54,796 --> 01:11:56,063
- Who?
- Lee Ye Eun.

1506
01:11:56,064 --> 01:11:57,431
- The girl with the serve?
- Yes.

1507
01:11:58,400 --> 01:12:00,234
Wait, she left her team?
Did she pack up and leave?

1508
01:12:00,702 --> 01:12:02,069
No, she filed for contract termination.

1509
01:12:02,337 --> 01:12:03,170
She did?

1510
01:12:06,541 --> 01:12:07,708
Coach?

1511
01:12:07,709 --> 01:12:08,642
Where are you?

1512
01:12:09,045 --> 01:12:10,310
I just arrived.

1513
01:12:11,646 --> 01:12:13,847
I'm at the Wonder Dogs tryouts now.

1514
01:12:14,983 --> 01:12:16,584
I'd like to try out too.

1515
01:12:17,853 --> 01:12:19,787
I'll grab my things and head right over.

1516
01:12:20,655 --> 01:12:22,022
Okay, then.

1517
01:12:22,023 --> 01:12:24,124
Take the earliest train you can...

1518
01:12:24,526 --> 01:12:27,895
and come to Sangnoksu
Kim Yeon Koung Gymnasium.

1519
01:12:28,897 --> 01:12:30,564
I'm exhausted today.

1520
01:12:30,899 --> 01:12:31,866
Hello.

1521
01:12:33,502 --> 01:12:34,436
Hello, everyone.

1522
01:12:35,670 --> 01:12:37,538
She's here. Is that Ye Sol?

1523
01:12:37,539 --> 01:12:39,006
- It's Ye Eun. Lee Ye Eun.
- Ye Eun?

1524
01:12:39,007 --> 01:12:40,008
(Lee Ye Eun, 175cm,)

1525
01:12:40,009 --> 01:12:42,209
(Korea Expressway Corporation Hi-Pass,
contract terminated at her request)

1526
01:12:42,778 --> 01:12:44,412
- Ye Eun, have you stretched?
- Yes.

1527
01:12:44,413 --> 01:12:45,680
Are you all warmed up?

1528
01:12:46,081 --> 01:12:49,484
- Did you warm up outside?
- I warmed up on the train on my way here.

1529
01:12:49,485 --> 01:12:50,851
She warmed up on the train.

1530
01:12:50,852 --> 01:12:52,787
She's really eager.

1531
01:12:52,788 --> 01:12:54,288
On the train?

1532
01:12:58,460 --> 01:13:00,963
Remember when Hi-Pass reverse-swept us?

1533
01:13:00,964 --> 01:13:02,396
I was with the Pink Spiders then.

1534
01:13:02,397 --> 01:13:05,033
Ye Eun came on late
and scored a service ace,

1535
01:13:05,034 --> 01:13:06,233
and Hi-Pass won.

1536
01:13:06,234 --> 01:13:07,101
- Really?
- Yes.

1537
01:13:07,102 --> 01:13:08,436
We got reverse-swept, remember?

1538
01:13:09,004 --> 01:13:09,937
We were in tears.

1539
01:13:12,241 --> 01:13:14,442
- You're here for the tryout, right?
- Yes.

1540
01:13:14,770 --> 01:13:15,670
This way, please.

1541
01:13:15,671 --> 01:13:16,671
(Reunited at the tryouts)

1542
01:13:16,832 --> 01:13:18,432
We have a few things to check.

1543
01:13:18,901 --> 01:13:20,435
It might be a little tough.

1544
01:13:20,569 --> 01:13:21,435
That's fine.

1545
01:13:21,436 --> 01:13:23,137
- Let's ease into it.
- Okay.

1546
01:13:23,138 --> 01:13:24,272
(The same tests as the other players.)

1547
01:13:24,273 --> 01:13:26,140
- Let's start with your serve.
- Okay.

1548
01:13:27,276 --> 01:13:29,377
(Target serve speed: 65km per hour)

1549
01:13:31,747 --> 01:13:32,747
That's fast.

1550
01:13:33,616 --> 01:13:34,416
What's the speed?

1551
01:13:34,717 --> 01:13:36,451
- The speed is 68km per hour.
- That's 68.

1552
01:13:38,554 --> 01:13:39,988
- Let's aim for that speed.
- It's 69km per hour.

1553
01:13:39,989 --> 01:13:41,222
Okay, good.

1554
01:13:41,891 --> 01:13:43,592
Our target is 65km per hour.

1555
01:13:43,726 --> 01:13:46,695
She's over 65. She hit 65 and 68.

1556
01:13:46,696 --> 01:13:47,662
(She passes the serve speed test.)

1557
01:13:47,897 --> 01:13:49,865
(Attack test)

1558
01:13:50,900 --> 01:13:51,967
That's it.

1559
01:13:54,804 --> 01:13:55,537
Okay.

1560
01:13:55,538 --> 01:13:56,972
(She scores past the blockers.)

1561
01:13:56,973 --> 01:13:57,806
Good!

1562
01:13:59,142 --> 01:14:00,342
Okay. Ready!

1563
01:14:00,343 --> 01:14:01,042
(Receiving test)

1564
01:14:01,744 --> 01:14:03,011
Mine!

1565
01:14:03,813 --> 01:14:04,646
Ready!

1566
01:14:04,914 --> 01:14:05,647
Mine!

1567
01:14:05,648 --> 01:14:07,115
(Right into the target zone)

1568
01:14:07,116 --> 01:14:08,249
Ready!

1569
01:14:08,717 --> 01:14:10,151
(Impressed)

1570
01:14:10,152 --> 01:14:11,452
Mine!

1571
01:14:12,321 --> 01:14:13,154
Ready!

1572
01:14:13,155 --> 01:14:17,059
(Lee Ye Eun, reception: plus 1 point)

1573
01:14:17,060 --> 01:14:17,959
Ready!

1574
01:14:18,294 --> 01:14:20,595
(Perfect reception)

1575
01:14:21,130 --> 01:14:22,797
She might actually get to play.

1576
01:14:23,199 --> 01:14:25,200
- Mine!
- Her reception is really good.

1577
01:14:26,769 --> 01:14:31,072
(Receiving had been
Coach Yeon Koung's biggest concern.)

1578
01:14:31,674 --> 01:14:33,141
But so far,

1579
01:14:33,142 --> 01:14:34,476
- she's in a class of her own.
- She's the best.

1580
01:14:34,477 --> 01:14:36,978
- She's even better than Yu Kyung.
- She's at that level.

1581
01:14:37,580 --> 01:14:38,947
Mine!

1582
01:14:38,948 --> 01:14:41,583
She could be
our team's go-to serve receiver.

1583
01:14:41,584 --> 01:14:42,551
(Accuracy beyond a libero)

1584
01:14:42,751 --> 01:14:43,818
Hello.

1585
01:14:44,320 --> 01:14:47,756
I'm Lee Ye Eun, and I'm here
to try out for the Wonder Dogs.

1586
01:14:48,824 --> 01:14:51,993
I told my team I wanted to leave,

1587
01:14:51,994 --> 01:14:54,095
and I left on my own terms.

1588
01:14:54,797 --> 01:14:57,265
The thing is, in the pro league,

1589
01:14:57,266 --> 01:15:00,835
there are so many players
who are better than me,

1590
01:15:01,170 --> 01:15:03,905
so I never really had
a chance to earn a starting spot.

1591
01:15:04,773 --> 01:15:07,375
I wanted to find a new opportunity
no matter what.

1592
01:15:07,376 --> 01:15:08,376
(Desperate for a new opportunity)

1593
01:15:09,011 --> 01:15:12,447
I applied because I wanted
to try everything I could.

1594
01:15:12,448 --> 01:15:14,048
(I'll try everything I can.)

1595
01:15:15,884 --> 01:15:19,687
(Most of the seats are now filled.)

1596
01:15:20,022 --> 01:15:21,122
How many spots are left?

1597
01:15:25,027 --> 01:15:26,528
- Three?
- Three left.

1598
01:15:26,529 --> 01:15:28,262
- Three spots left.
- That's still three.

1599
01:15:29,999 --> 01:15:33,435
(Three Season One Wonder Dogs
have yet to arrive.)

1600
01:15:33,436 --> 01:15:35,003
Things are getting serious now.

1601
01:15:35,004 --> 01:15:36,071
- Right?
- I know.

1602
01:15:41,777 --> 01:15:45,046
(One final libero spot)

1603
01:15:49,718 --> 01:15:51,485
The libero spot is a tough call too.

1604
01:15:51,954 --> 01:15:55,456
We already picked Seo Yu Kyung
as our first choice.

1605
01:15:56,191 --> 01:15:58,626
Now it's between Koo Hye In
and Chae Seon Ah.

1606
01:15:59,862 --> 01:16:01,529
(Pinpoint reception)

1607
01:16:01,930 --> 01:16:03,964
(Season One's Koo Hye In)

1608
01:16:04,500 --> 01:16:06,568
(A veteran known for her steady play)

1609
01:16:06,769 --> 01:16:07,869
(Chae Seon Ah, 15-year pro veteran)

1610
01:16:07,870 --> 01:16:08,770
Nice!

1611
01:16:09,305 --> 01:16:10,205
Go!

1612
01:16:10,206 --> 01:16:13,575
(Their strong defense...)

1613
01:16:13,576 --> 01:16:17,178
(makes for fierce competition.)

1614
01:16:20,349 --> 01:16:21,316
The libero decision is tough.

1615
01:16:22,484 --> 01:16:23,451
This is tough.

1616
01:16:23,452 --> 01:16:26,287
(Who will take the final libero spot?)

1617
01:16:41,303 --> 01:16:42,336
Someone is coming.

1618
01:16:42,504 --> 01:16:44,305
- It's Seon Ah.
- What?

1619
01:16:44,306 --> 01:16:46,841
(Chae Seon Ah, 176cm,
Pohang Sports Council)

1620
01:16:48,177 --> 01:16:50,311
- Hello.
- Hello.

1621
01:16:53,682 --> 01:16:54,548
Oh, my!

1622
01:16:55,217 --> 01:16:57,351
I really struggled with the decision.

1623
01:16:57,753 --> 01:17:00,388
It weighed on me,

1624
01:17:01,423 --> 01:17:03,925
but I still had to be objective.

1625
01:17:04,593 --> 01:17:06,661
- Hye In isn't making an impact, is she?
- No.

1626
01:17:06,662 --> 01:17:07,795
- Hye In.
- She's not.

1627
01:17:07,796 --> 01:17:08,863
What's wrong with Hye In?

1628
01:17:10,699 --> 01:17:11,566
(A mistake)

1629
01:17:13,469 --> 01:17:14,436
What's going on with Hye In?

1630
01:17:17,111 --> 01:17:19,011
(Missed free ball)

1631
01:17:19,297 --> 01:17:23,330
- Did you catch that missed free ball?
- Yeah.

1632
01:17:24,390 --> 01:17:26,490
(Koo Hye In: minus 1 for defense)

1633
01:17:26,817 --> 01:17:28,316
(Another miss, and another)

1634
01:17:28,317 --> 01:17:29,946
That's another deduction.

1635
01:17:30,317 --> 01:17:33,217
(Hye In's shaky form)

1636
01:17:33,817 --> 01:17:35,585
Her touch is off today.

1637
01:17:35,604 --> 01:17:36,857
(Coach Kim deep in thought)

1638
01:17:37,250 --> 01:17:39,882
I needed someone
with a steadier floor game.

1639
01:17:39,883 --> 01:17:42,349
And veteran poise.

1640
01:17:42,350 --> 01:17:44,350
Chae Seon Ah showed she brings both.

1641
01:17:47,383 --> 01:17:50,417
(Locked-down defense)

1642
01:17:50,717 --> 01:17:54,317
(Clean transition out of system)

1643
01:17:54,683 --> 01:17:56,648
When I dig the free ball,

1644
01:17:56,673 --> 01:17:57,807
load up for a pipe attack.

1645
01:17:57,850 --> 01:17:59,683
Free ball! Back row, get ready!

1646
01:18:00,683 --> 01:18:04,122
(Vocal leadership anchoring the floor)

1647
01:18:04,542 --> 01:18:07,750
(Seasoned veteran presence)

1648
01:18:08,083 --> 01:18:12,149
Watching Seung Ju and Na Yeon
compete last season...

1649
01:18:12,150 --> 01:18:15,217
lit that fire in me to try out.

1650
01:18:15,761 --> 01:18:20,095
At my age, I feel like this is
my final run at a comeback.

1651
01:18:20,528 --> 01:18:22,598
So I want to leave everything
on the court.

1652
01:18:23,494 --> 01:18:24,833
I want to show what I've still got.

1653
01:18:28,361 --> 01:18:34,260
(Final setter vacancy)

1654
01:18:34,261 --> 01:18:36,745
Now comes the agonizing choice at setter.

1655
01:18:37,628 --> 01:18:40,861
Kim Da Sol is a lock.

1656
01:18:41,494 --> 01:18:44,394
It comes down
to Ha Hyo Rim versus Lee Jin.

1657
01:18:45,994 --> 01:18:47,593
Hyo Rim plays with far more control.

1658
01:18:47,594 --> 01:18:51,961
(Ha Hyo Rim: rock-solid playmaker)

1659
01:18:52,928 --> 01:18:54,493
Hyo Rim stays composed out there.

1660
01:18:54,494 --> 01:18:56,031
Lee Jin, on the other hand,

1661
01:18:57,494 --> 01:19:01,027
has great tempo chasing down high passes
and adjusting on the run.

1662
01:19:01,028 --> 01:19:03,928
(Lee Jin: explosive playmaking setter)

1663
01:19:04,194 --> 01:19:05,160
Her offensive rhythm is crisp.

1664
01:19:05,185 --> 01:19:06,852
(A delivery that caught the eye
of Coach Lee Hyo Hee)

1665
01:19:12,861 --> 01:19:13,728
(Gasps)

1666
01:19:21,394 --> 01:19:24,327
(Ha Hyo Rim, 172 cm, Suwon Special City)

1667
01:19:24,328 --> 01:19:25,427
She looks sharp.

1668
01:19:26,937 --> 01:19:28,603
(Bows)

1669
01:19:28,628 --> 01:19:30,400
- Look at her, all awkward.
- I know.

1670
01:19:30,425 --> 01:19:31,500
It surprised me.

1671
01:19:34,028 --> 01:19:36,728
My pick went to Ha Hyo Rim because...

1672
01:19:37,161 --> 01:19:38,494
she provides consistency.

1673
01:19:39,494 --> 01:19:41,494
Over here!

1674
01:19:42,194 --> 01:19:43,161
My bad!

1675
01:19:44,094 --> 01:19:47,594
(Like Hye In, Jin looked unsettled.)

1676
01:19:50,061 --> 01:19:51,754
She can't seem to command
the ball cleanly.

1677
01:19:52,328 --> 01:19:53,894
(Hyo Rim, meanwhile...)

1678
01:19:54,847 --> 01:19:58,714
(A high ball)

1679
01:19:59,461 --> 01:20:02,628
(A clutch bump set)

1680
01:20:03,128 --> 01:20:04,860
(Whatever the breakdown,)

1681
01:20:04,861 --> 01:20:10,394
(her touch never wavers.)

1682
01:20:12,194 --> 01:20:15,027
Hyo Rim kept the offense steady
throughout the run.

1683
01:20:15,028 --> 01:20:20,260
I need her to be that rock
for this lineup.

1684
01:20:20,261 --> 01:20:23,193
I came in hunting for consistency,

1685
01:20:23,194 --> 01:20:24,561
and she delivered it.

1686
01:20:26,128 --> 01:20:27,928
That leaves one roster spot, right?

1687
01:20:28,367 --> 01:20:30,600
Yeah, one final player.

1688
01:20:30,628 --> 01:20:32,028
Just one opening left.

1689
01:20:32,928 --> 01:20:33,827
One seat?

1690
01:20:33,828 --> 01:20:35,794
(One spot remaining)

1691
01:20:36,194 --> 01:20:38,327
(Glances)

1692
01:20:38,328 --> 01:20:40,135
We haven't named an opposite hitter yet.

1693
01:20:41,028 --> 01:20:42,228
We're missing our right.

1694
01:20:42,961 --> 01:20:44,761
- Good catch.
- We still need an OP.

1695
01:20:46,394 --> 01:20:48,360
Could it be Young In?

1696
01:20:48,361 --> 01:20:49,361
(Could it be...)

1697
01:20:51,061 --> 01:20:54,393
(Opposite Spiker)

1698
01:20:54,394 --> 01:20:57,193
At OP, it's down to Park Hyeon Ju
and Yoon Young In.

1699
01:20:57,194 --> 01:20:58,486
(Park Hyeon Ju vs. Yoon Young In)

1700
01:21:01,428 --> 01:21:03,993
(In attacking firepower,)

1701
01:21:03,994 --> 01:21:10,894
(it was a dead heat.)

1702
01:21:11,994 --> 01:21:16,494
(Who claims the final spot?)

1703
01:21:22,994 --> 01:21:23,828
Who takes it?

1704
01:21:27,861 --> 01:21:28,660
Who is it?

1705
01:21:28,661 --> 01:21:31,093
(Yoon Young In, 177 cm,
Suwon Special City)

1706
01:21:31,094 --> 01:21:32,128
It's Young In!

1707
01:21:33,994 --> 01:21:36,661
(Smiles)

1708
01:21:36,894 --> 01:21:38,028
So good to have her back.

1709
01:21:42,894 --> 01:21:44,427
(Final roster spot: Yoon Young In)

1710
01:21:44,428 --> 01:21:48,928
Every single player showed flashes
during tryouts.

1711
01:21:49,304 --> 01:21:52,069
Making the final cut for the OP
was agonizing.

1712
01:21:52,094 --> 01:21:53,661
I wrestled with it constantly.

1713
01:21:54,928 --> 01:21:56,928
- In the end, Young In has the edge.
- Young In?

1714
01:21:57,161 --> 01:22:00,360
Whether attacking or putting up a wall...

1715
01:22:00,385 --> 01:22:03,552
- Young In's net defense is huge.
- She's a good blocker.

1716
01:22:06,728 --> 01:22:08,293
(Shutting down attacks...)

1717
01:22:08,294 --> 01:22:11,527
(just as well as putting balls away)

1718
01:22:11,528 --> 01:22:16,760
Young In proved she can
control the net and finish points.

1719
01:22:16,761 --> 01:22:18,193
We made the right call.

1720
01:22:18,218 --> 01:22:19,452
(A two-way weapon at the net)

1721
01:22:22,328 --> 01:22:25,761
(13 players selected)

1722
01:22:26,761 --> 01:22:28,561
Only 4 veterans from Season 1
made the cut.

1723
01:22:29,961 --> 01:22:31,727
- It hurts to see, honestly.
- Right?

1724
01:22:31,728 --> 01:22:36,328
I really wanted Hye In and Jin
to be part of this group.

1725
01:22:38,694 --> 01:22:41,160
We have to take the court immediately.

1726
01:22:41,161 --> 01:22:42,260
Which forces us to prioritize...

1727
01:22:42,261 --> 01:22:45,094
immediate poise
and what they can offer right now.

1728
01:22:46,894 --> 01:22:49,861
Those two piled up
too many unforced errors out there.

1729
01:22:50,428 --> 01:22:51,627
It wasn't clean enough.

1730
01:22:51,628 --> 01:22:52,427
That docked them crucial points.

1731
01:22:52,428 --> 01:22:54,069
Hye In, that was a tough look.

1732
01:22:54,394 --> 01:22:56,893
If this program is truly gunning
for pro status,

1733
01:22:56,894 --> 01:22:58,561
we have to produce wins.

1734
01:23:00,261 --> 01:23:01,961
Which means being cold and objective.

1735
01:23:02,328 --> 01:23:05,528
(Lee Jin and Koo Hye In miss the cut.)

1736
01:23:08,828 --> 01:23:12,761
Truthfully, I was worried
about how they'd take it.

1737
01:23:14,061 --> 01:23:17,361
I'm pulling Jin and Hye In aside
for a private talk.

1738
01:23:18,794 --> 01:23:21,828
(After tryouts)

1739
01:23:22,528 --> 01:23:25,328
(Yeon Koung waits to speak
with Jin and Hye In.)

1740
01:23:31,361 --> 01:23:32,428
Take a seat, Jin.

1741
01:23:38,461 --> 01:23:40,161
This is brutal.

1742
01:23:43,894 --> 01:23:45,661
(Hesitates)

1743
01:23:49,394 --> 01:23:51,194
You know,

1744
01:23:53,194 --> 01:23:57,194
after going back and forth
with the staff...

1745
01:23:58,794 --> 01:24:00,128
it turns out...

1746
01:24:00,661 --> 01:24:03,961
we won't be able to bring you along
for Season Two.

1747
01:24:04,428 --> 01:24:07,294
I wanted to deliver that face-to-face.

1748
01:24:12,194 --> 01:24:18,694
(Delivering the hard truth in person)

1749
01:24:21,328 --> 01:24:22,758
- It really breaks my heart.
- Yes.

1750
01:24:26,828 --> 01:24:28,697
I've developed such a soft spot
for you two.

1751
01:24:30,928 --> 01:24:33,561
Surviving Season One side by side
forged a real bond.

1752
01:24:36,094 --> 01:24:37,894
How did tryouts feel to you?

1753
01:24:43,061 --> 01:24:45,761
They felt good.

1754
01:24:48,094 --> 01:24:50,094
I had fun out there.

1755
01:24:52,161 --> 01:24:54,056
Just being able to play again.

1756
01:24:54,694 --> 01:24:55,624
So it was a good day.

1757
01:24:59,494 --> 01:25:01,128
I just came up short.

1758
01:25:02,594 --> 01:25:04,193
- You felt you wouldn't make it?
- Yeah.

1759
01:25:04,194 --> 01:25:05,534
Right from the opening whistle?

1760
01:25:05,561 --> 01:25:06,394
Why?

1761
01:25:06,894 --> 01:25:09,428
Everyone else was playing
like their lives depended on it.

1762
01:25:11,161 --> 01:25:12,427
Seon Ah looked incredible.

1763
01:25:12,428 --> 01:25:15,460
Yu Kyung was lights-out too.

1764
01:25:15,461 --> 01:25:16,945
It made me lose my nerve a bit.

1765
01:25:20,661 --> 01:25:23,260
I think you need to sit down and unpack...

1766
01:25:23,261 --> 01:25:26,460
what truly led to this outcome.

1767
01:25:26,461 --> 01:25:30,694
Don't chalk it up
to circumstances or bad luck.

1768
01:25:32,161 --> 01:25:35,628
Look in the mirror first.

1769
01:25:35,646 --> 01:25:38,459
(Something she should figure out
from within)

1770
01:25:39,828 --> 01:25:41,436
Another window will open up.

1771
01:25:43,928 --> 01:25:45,374
Your story isn't over.

1772
01:25:47,528 --> 01:25:49,678
Make sure you're actually ready
when that call comes.

1773
01:25:49,861 --> 01:25:51,994
Come back tougher.

1774
01:25:54,228 --> 01:25:56,184
I hope next time around...

1775
01:25:56,861 --> 01:26:01,628
I can show you a completely
different player.

1776
01:26:10,261 --> 01:26:12,528
- You're staying on the court, right?
- Of course.

1777
01:26:19,361 --> 01:26:20,994
- You've done great.
- Thank you.

1778
01:26:24,294 --> 01:26:25,194
What is it?

1779
01:26:26,067 --> 01:26:27,622
- What are you doing?
- Give me a hug.

1780
01:26:38,161 --> 01:26:41,828
Having to break the bad news myself...

1781
01:26:42,361 --> 01:26:44,594
never gets any easier.

1782
01:26:45,561 --> 01:26:48,793
It had been so long
since I saw them back in uniform.

1783
01:26:48,794 --> 01:26:50,961
All I wanted was to give them a nod...

1784
01:26:51,328 --> 01:26:53,461
and tell them they did great.

1785
01:26:54,628 --> 01:26:55,877
Jin didn't make the cut?

1786
01:26:56,528 --> 01:26:57,960
Jin's rhythm was off today.

1787
01:26:57,961 --> 01:26:59,781
Hye In couldn't find her footing either.

1788
01:26:59,994 --> 01:27:02,361
- Hye In doesn't stand out.
- No.

1789
01:27:02,928 --> 01:27:06,161
(Heartbroken more than anyone else)

1790
01:27:08,661 --> 01:27:09,493
I'm sorry.

1791
01:27:09,494 --> 01:27:11,660
Hye In, this isn't the time to apologize!

1792
01:27:12,694 --> 01:27:14,493
(Her raw dedication outshone everyone.)

1793
01:27:14,494 --> 01:27:15,763
Keep your head up.

1794
01:27:15,788 --> 01:27:17,689
(The players have grown,)

1795
01:27:19,421 --> 01:27:21,047
(and the coach has grown with them.)

1796
01:27:22,290 --> 01:27:24,034
(Which makes parting ways
cut even deeper.)

1797
01:27:24,059 --> 01:27:25,359
- Give it everything you've got.
- Will do.

1798
01:27:25,360 --> 01:27:26,742
You know how it is, right?

1799
01:27:27,529 --> 01:27:30,397
Having to make those tough calls,

1800
01:27:30,433 --> 01:27:33,382
and carrying the full weight of the team
on your shoulders...

1801
01:27:35,305 --> 01:27:38,039
It weighs on you.

1802
01:27:40,308 --> 01:27:41,174
Still,

1803
01:27:43,278 --> 01:27:45,066
I've got to power through it.

1804
01:27:45,331 --> 01:27:47,195
That's the job when you're head coach.

1805
01:27:48,517 --> 01:27:50,365
I just have to leave it all out there.

1806
01:27:54,556 --> 01:27:56,457
It feels like an endless trial.

1807
01:28:04,900 --> 01:28:06,167
Hello.

1808
01:28:06,168 --> 01:28:07,335
(Rookie Coach Kim Yeon Koung)

1809
01:28:07,336 --> 01:28:11,005
(Seasoned Coach Kim Yeon Koung)

1810
01:28:11,173 --> 01:28:13,040
- Hello.
- Hello.

1811
01:28:13,041 --> 01:28:14,623
Hello.

1812
01:28:17,012 --> 01:28:19,547
(A stacked new coaching staff)

1813
01:28:23,218 --> 01:28:26,620
(The Wonder Dogs assemble.)

1814
01:28:27,589 --> 01:28:30,958
We're holding
the official kickoff ceremony at a hotel.

1815
01:28:31,760 --> 01:28:32,727
Nice.

1816
01:28:35,621 --> 01:28:36,745
Here we go.

1817
01:28:39,468 --> 01:28:43,018
Welcome, everyone,
to the Wonder Dogs' 2026 season.

1818
01:28:53,248 --> 01:28:55,564
We're a squad of underdogs,

1819
01:28:56,651 --> 01:28:59,987
players waived by pro clubs,
veterans out of retirement,

1820
01:29:00,489 --> 01:29:04,992
and free agents fighting
for one more shot on the court.

1821
01:29:06,461 --> 01:29:08,327
Alongside Coach Kim Yeon Koung,

1822
01:29:08,631 --> 01:29:11,046
every single one of them is ready to turn
from underdogs into wonders.

1823
01:29:12,267 --> 01:29:14,768
Our name is the Pilseung Wonder Dogs.

1824
01:29:16,071 --> 01:29:18,553
And the ultimate goal
of the Pilseung Wonder Dogs is...

1825
01:29:19,208 --> 01:29:21,676
to establish the league's
eighth professional franchise.

1826
01:29:31,653 --> 01:29:33,235
- What's that?
- Is that a QR code?

1827
01:29:33,655 --> 01:29:35,856
- A QR code?
- Is that really a QR code?

1828
01:29:40,328 --> 01:29:41,943
Are we supposed to scan it?

1829
01:29:46,802 --> 01:29:47,835
Pilseung.

1830
01:29:47,836 --> 01:29:49,203
Wonder Dogs.

1831
01:29:49,204 --> 01:29:51,072
(Pilseung Wonder Dogs)

1832
01:29:52,440 --> 01:29:56,209
This season, we're putting
our name on the block.

1833
01:30:01,683 --> 01:30:04,285
(Pilseung Wonder Dogs)

1834
01:30:05,320 --> 01:30:07,855
(A Chemical, B Securities, C Partners)

1835
01:30:10,091 --> 01:30:12,793
(A corporation ready
to take ownership of the club)

1836
01:30:14,729 --> 01:30:17,130
(We are scouting a franchise owner
for the Wonder Dogs.)

1837
01:30:17,332 --> 01:30:18,599
Have you lost your mind?

1838
01:30:18,800 --> 01:30:19,833
(Not in the slightest)

1839
01:30:19,834 --> 01:30:21,249
Why is that popping up again?

1840
01:30:23,538 --> 01:30:25,487
What are you two cooking up over there?

1841
01:30:25,807 --> 01:30:28,409
(We came to build a real franchise.)

1842
01:30:29,277 --> 01:30:31,660
We started out
as just an unscripted TV show.

1843
01:30:31,913 --> 01:30:33,728
Do you genuinely think
we can launch a pro club?

1844
01:30:34,783 --> 01:30:36,650
It's possible.

1845
01:30:37,018 --> 01:30:40,620
It's absolutely doable, and beyond that,

1846
01:30:40,621 --> 01:30:42,204
I genuinely want you to pull it off.

1847
01:30:42,958 --> 01:30:46,427
(The first-ever pro team born
from an entertainment show)

1848
01:30:46,875 --> 01:30:52,875
(Wonder Dogs)

1849
01:30:52,900 --> 01:30:54,001
That gives me goosebumps.

1850
01:30:54,436 --> 01:30:56,952
It'll be massive if it actually happens.

1851
01:31:00,475 --> 01:31:02,042
(This is bigger than just volleyball.)

1852
01:31:02,978 --> 01:31:04,612
(One single ball,)

1853
01:31:05,447 --> 01:31:06,414
(loaded with their dreams)

1854
01:31:06,451 --> 01:31:07,891
You've got this, no question.

1855
01:31:21,363 --> 01:31:24,532
Victory belongs to the Wonder Dogs.

1856
01:31:30,572 --> 01:31:35,476
(Wonder Dogs)

1857
01:31:36,211 --> 01:31:39,346
(Open Call for Franchise Owner)

1858
01:31:40,315 --> 01:31:41,663
An open call?

1859
01:31:42,717 --> 01:31:43,684
What is this?

1860
01:31:46,454 --> 01:31:48,688
(Open Call for Franchise Owner)

1861
01:31:48,689 --> 01:31:50,424
(Inviting corporate partners
to step up...)

1862
01:31:50,425 --> 01:31:52,993
(and own the Wonder Dogs,
the 8th pro club.)

1863
01:31:52,994 --> 01:31:55,395
("Sponsor" Wonder Dogs)

1864
01:31:56,097 --> 01:32:02,736
(Looking for the partner
who will build this team with us.)

1865
01:32:09,511 --> 01:32:10,625
Seventy-seven days?

1866
01:32:10,779 --> 01:32:13,347
Our window to prove we belong...

1867
01:32:13,581 --> 01:32:17,132
closes on December 27,
our projected finale date.

1868
01:32:18,553 --> 01:32:21,455
That gives us exactly 77 days...

1869
01:32:21,823 --> 01:32:23,538
starting from today's premiere.

1870
01:32:25,860 --> 01:32:28,777
If no corporate owner
steps up to claim us,

1871
01:32:29,464 --> 01:32:30,812
there won't be...

1872
01:32:31,666 --> 01:32:32,633
another season.

1873
01:32:35,179 --> 01:32:38,815
So flashing raw talent
on the court isn't enough.

1874
01:32:38,840 --> 01:32:42,490
We have to prove we have what it takes
to operate as a legitimate pro franchise.

1875
01:32:45,146 --> 01:32:46,379
Seventy-seven?

1876
01:32:46,715 --> 01:32:47,862
Double lucky seven?

1877
01:32:48,783 --> 01:32:50,231
Maybe we actually have a shot.

1878
01:32:50,752 --> 01:32:52,367
Let's make something happen out here.

1879
01:32:52,787 --> 01:32:56,423
Since I'm gearing up to play
for the eighth team...

1880
01:32:56,658 --> 01:32:58,493
I'm throwing everything I have into this,

1881
01:32:58,494 --> 01:33:01,076
and I'll help get this franchise
off the ground.

1882
01:33:01,897 --> 01:33:02,963
We'll show them.

1883
01:33:03,198 --> 01:33:04,899
I think we can do it.

1884
01:33:10,038 --> 01:33:11,219
That scared me.

1885
01:33:12,841 --> 01:33:13,707
What's going on?

1886
01:33:14,009 --> 01:33:15,290
Total shocker.

1887
01:33:29,591 --> 01:33:34,361
(Wonder Dogs Mock Draft)

1888
01:33:34,829 --> 01:33:35,829
Another evaluation?

1889
01:33:36,398 --> 01:33:37,331
Oh, man.

1890
01:33:38,400 --> 01:33:39,914
The moment of truth is here.

1891
01:33:41,870 --> 01:33:45,253
Seeing that setup immediately took me back
to the high school draft hall.

1892
01:33:46,174 --> 01:33:47,808
At official drafts,

1893
01:33:48,276 --> 01:33:51,278
that's exactly how the banners are hung.

1894
01:33:54,082 --> 01:33:56,584
(In fact, this venue is...)

1895
01:33:57,952 --> 01:34:00,687
(September 5, 2025)

1896
01:34:01,156 --> 01:34:06,827
(The official rookie draft was staged
right here at Hotel M.)

1897
01:34:08,029 --> 01:34:09,265
(The rookie draft gathers...)

1898
01:34:09,289 --> 01:34:14,101
(top high school prospects
and undrafted hopefuls.)

1899
01:34:14,802 --> 01:34:18,038
(Following franchise
front-office deliberations,)

1900
01:34:18,773 --> 01:34:21,808
(the draft order is settled by lottery.)

1901
01:34:23,111 --> 01:34:27,815
(Each team makes its selection.)

1902
01:34:30,051 --> 01:34:31,518
Please give these players a chance,

1903
01:34:31,519 --> 01:34:33,320
knowing how much blood and sweat
they've poured into this.

1904
01:34:34,155 --> 01:34:36,857
(For the families looking on,)

1905
01:34:38,793 --> 01:34:43,397
(and above all for the athletes,
this room is sheer desperation.)

1906
01:34:44,933 --> 01:34:47,067
(In this very room,)

1907
01:34:48,137 --> 01:34:51,237
(they find themselves facing
the draft once more.)

1908
01:34:54,042 --> 01:34:56,443
I was breaking out in a cold sweat.

1909
01:34:57,344 --> 01:35:01,214
I never imagined I'd go through the draft
a second time.

1910
01:35:10,192 --> 01:35:12,659
I got passed over
in this exact room before.

1911
01:35:13,061 --> 01:35:14,909
That memory kept flashing through my head.

1912
01:35:15,330 --> 01:35:17,531
Going through the draft again
is just brutal.

1913
01:35:18,700 --> 01:35:19,667
That's...

1914
01:35:23,938 --> 01:35:25,640
(During practice one year ago)

1915
01:35:25,641 --> 01:35:28,008
Keep this between us,

1916
01:35:28,409 --> 01:35:30,844
but I'm thinking
about declaring for the draft.

1917
01:35:30,845 --> 01:35:32,293
Did you submit your papers?

1918
01:35:32,914 --> 01:35:34,114
Yeah, yesterday.

1919
01:35:34,139 --> 01:35:36,416
Wait, is this your first time
entering since high school?

1920
01:35:36,417 --> 01:35:37,918
- Yeah.
- Has it been eight whole years?

1921
01:35:37,919 --> 01:35:39,019
Eight whole years.

1922
01:35:39,020 --> 01:35:40,120
(Eight years in the semi-pro
corporate league)

1923
01:35:40,121 --> 01:35:41,088
That's great.

1924
01:35:42,490 --> 01:35:44,458
(September 5, 2025)

1925
01:35:44,993 --> 01:35:48,028
(She found the grit
to take a second shot at the draft.)

1926
01:35:48,463 --> 01:35:51,832
(Her parents)

1927
01:35:52,867 --> 01:35:56,437
(Even sportscaster Lee Ho Geun
showed up courtside to back her.)

1928
01:36:00,742 --> 01:36:03,110
(The opening round picks began.)

1929
01:36:04,512 --> 01:36:07,214
She's officially wearing the colors.
Huge congratulations.

1930
01:36:07,215 --> 01:36:09,664
That jersey suits her so well.

1931
01:36:12,387 --> 01:36:15,222
(From that moment on,)

1932
01:36:17,492 --> 01:36:24,448
(she just kept on applauding
and cheering for other players.)

1933
01:36:27,468 --> 01:36:33,039
(Then came the final pick.)

1934
01:36:38,379 --> 01:36:42,617
(In the end, her name was never called.)

1935
01:36:42,618 --> 01:36:44,517
Congratulations!

1936
01:36:47,088 --> 01:36:49,122
(Commemorative photo shoot
of the drafted prospects)

1937
01:36:49,123 --> 01:36:51,858
That concludes the women's rookie draft.

1938
01:36:51,859 --> 01:36:56,230
Congratulations to all the players
taking their first strides into the pros.

1939
01:36:56,364 --> 01:36:58,366
Wishing you our absolute best.

1940
01:36:58,833 --> 01:37:00,591
I'm so sorry.
You made the trip out here for nothing.

1941
01:37:00,615 --> 01:37:01,901
Don't even say that.

1942
01:37:03,404 --> 01:37:05,238
I'm so sorry, producer.

1943
01:37:07,108 --> 01:37:09,343
Thank you for everything.

1944
01:37:15,076 --> 01:37:16,909
Let's go, Mom.

1945
01:37:28,618 --> 01:37:31,818
(For one member, the draft dredges up
two painful memories.)

1946
01:37:34,412 --> 01:37:39,276
(Target: launch the 8th franchise,
which means looking reality in the eye)

1947
01:37:39,918 --> 01:37:41,817
(We asked actual pro personnel...)

1948
01:37:41,818 --> 01:37:44,551
(if this squad has what it takes
to compete in the league.)

1949
01:37:44,851 --> 01:37:45,718
What?

1950
01:37:49,884 --> 01:37:53,222
Front-office staff from actual pro clubs
evaluating us live...

1951
01:37:53,246 --> 01:37:54,484
caught me off guard.

1952
01:37:58,451 --> 01:38:03,251
We will now begin the 2026 Mock Draft
for the Wonder Dogs roster.

1953
01:38:04,584 --> 01:38:05,801
For today's mock draft,

1954
01:38:05,825 --> 01:38:09,117
active front-office decision-makers
from pro clubs will participate...

1955
01:38:09,118 --> 01:38:11,436
and state whether they would
actually draft each player...

1956
01:38:11,460 --> 01:38:12,854
if this were a sanctioned draft.

1957
01:38:13,218 --> 01:38:15,417
The Wonder Dogs players
will now be evaluated.

1958
01:38:15,418 --> 01:38:18,317
(The faces and voices
of franchise officials have been altered.)

1959
01:38:18,318 --> 01:38:20,484
(Glances)

1960
01:38:20,751 --> 01:38:24,499
It looks like other front offices
came fully prepared.

1961
01:38:34,118 --> 01:38:36,918
(Joining the three pro clubs...)

1962
01:38:39,818 --> 01:38:41,737
(Lee Jung Chul:
former national team head coach)

1963
01:38:41,761 --> 01:38:42,984
(Former IBK Altos head coach)

1964
01:38:43,551 --> 01:38:46,151
(Chang So Yun:
former AI Peppers head coach)

1965
01:38:46,918 --> 01:38:49,918
(Han Yoo Mi: London Olympian,
former AI Peppers coach)

1966
01:38:50,618 --> 01:38:53,551
(A veteran trio of former pro coaches)

1967
01:38:54,784 --> 01:38:57,851
Do these Wonder Dogs players
truly have pro potential?

1968
01:38:58,184 --> 01:39:00,417
Each franchise panel
will deliberate and...

1969
01:39:00,418 --> 01:39:04,418
raise their O/X paddles
to declare their consensus.

1970
01:39:07,118 --> 01:39:09,351
We'll draw the first name.

1971
01:39:21,151 --> 01:39:22,618
Baek Chae Rim.

1972
01:39:23,084 --> 01:39:26,718
(Baek Chae Rim: OH, 173 cm,
Suwon Special City)

1973
01:39:27,518 --> 01:39:28,850
She's a solid player.

1974
01:39:28,851 --> 01:39:30,318
Baek Chae Rim has real upside.

1975
01:39:31,184 --> 01:39:33,350
Her fundamentals are clean,
and her vertical is explosive.

1976
01:39:33,351 --> 01:39:34,803
She has great hang time.

1977
01:39:36,018 --> 01:39:38,473
She plays with high volleyball IQ
and great motor.

1978
01:39:39,718 --> 01:39:42,618
However...

1979
01:39:49,384 --> 01:39:51,386
Why throw an X after all that praise?

1980
01:39:53,551 --> 01:39:55,123
I just don't know...

1981
01:39:55,684 --> 01:39:57,258
if she moves the needle at the pro level.

1982
01:39:58,190 --> 01:39:59,557
Her finishing power
is a bit underwhelming,

1983
01:39:59,984 --> 01:40:01,851
and her blocking isn't quite there.

1984
01:40:02,284 --> 01:40:04,432
She's capped out
as a very solid semi-pro player.

1985
01:40:06,384 --> 01:40:08,203
Her attacking efficiency
sits around 16 percent.

1986
01:40:08,651 --> 01:40:09,783
That's not efficient enough.

1987
01:40:09,784 --> 01:40:12,218
(Attack efficiency: Pyo Seung Ju,
Enkhsoyol, Baek Chae Rim)

1988
01:40:12,684 --> 01:40:15,083
If she's aiming to knock
on pro doors again,

1989
01:40:15,084 --> 01:40:16,411
I'd have to advise against it.

1990
01:40:20,718 --> 01:40:21,518
Well.

1991
01:40:22,718 --> 01:40:25,118
For the Wonder Dogs, absolutely.

1992
01:40:26,284 --> 01:40:29,550
When building
a top-tier pro roster, though,

1993
01:40:29,551 --> 01:40:31,484
she falls just short of the mark.

1994
01:40:32,451 --> 01:40:34,884
I'd pass as well.

1995
01:40:36,684 --> 01:40:38,851
Would your franchise draft Baek Chae Rim?

1996
01:40:39,918 --> 01:40:41,684
Here is our consensus evaluation.

1997
01:40:57,351 --> 01:40:58,218
Moving on,

1998
01:41:00,484 --> 01:41:01,918
we have Ji Min Kyeong.

1999
01:41:02,851 --> 01:41:06,351
(Ji Min Kyeong: OH, 183 cm, free agent)

2000
01:41:07,118 --> 01:41:10,818
She was a dominant force
back in middle and high school.

2001
01:41:13,718 --> 01:41:15,584
A blue-chip rookie prospect.

2002
01:41:17,118 --> 01:41:20,384
(Selected 2nd overall
in Round 1 of the rookie draft)

2003
01:41:20,930 --> 01:41:23,897
(Crowned Rookie of the Year at age 18)

2004
01:41:24,751 --> 01:41:26,748
Going second overall
in the opening round speaks for itself.

2005
01:41:26,884 --> 01:41:28,149
She carried massive upside.

2006
01:41:28,384 --> 01:41:29,284
Definitely.

2007
01:41:30,318 --> 01:41:31,218
The problem is...

2008
01:41:32,018 --> 01:41:35,484
the persistent injury red flags.

2009
01:41:36,418 --> 01:41:39,761
If she were still young and fully healthy,
she'd be an automatic draft pick.

2010
01:41:42,451 --> 01:41:46,484
I'm painfully aware
that my knee is my biggest liability.

2011
01:41:47,751 --> 01:41:50,718
(A once-promising blue-chip talent)

2012
01:41:51,618 --> 01:41:53,283
(Star Rookie Derailed
by Lingering Knee Issues)

2013
01:41:53,284 --> 01:41:55,350
(Ji Min Kyeong Undergoes
Left Knee Reconstruction)

2014
01:41:55,351 --> 01:41:57,483
Right when I feel like I'm finally
rounding into form,

2015
01:41:57,484 --> 01:41:59,384
the pain flares up again.

2016
01:41:59,784 --> 01:42:02,550
That crushing hopelessness...

2017
01:42:02,551 --> 01:42:04,050
made every single day harder to bear.

2018
01:42:04,051 --> 01:42:05,051
(A protracted slump)

2019
01:42:06,551 --> 01:42:09,951
(Eventually waived by the franchise)

2020
01:42:10,484 --> 01:42:11,484
Realistically,

2021
01:42:12,851 --> 01:42:15,383
even if we invest time and develop her,

2022
01:42:15,384 --> 01:42:17,165
can she still take
that massive developmental leap?

2023
01:42:17,451 --> 01:42:18,733
In her mid-to-late twenties?

2024
01:42:18,984 --> 01:42:20,051
I just don't see it.

2025
01:42:21,418 --> 01:42:25,451
A frame with that height, power,
and baseline fundamentals is rare.

2026
01:42:27,384 --> 01:42:28,518
At this point, though,

2027
01:42:29,418 --> 01:42:31,145
she's just a reminder of past potential.

2028
01:42:31,284 --> 01:42:32,118
Exactly.

2029
01:42:35,830 --> 01:42:38,793
(Franchise C, Franchise B,
Franchise A, Franchise Advisors)

2030
01:42:38,818 --> 01:42:40,521
Another unanimous sweep of X's?

2031
01:42:44,618 --> 01:42:47,629
She got stuffed repeatedly
by high school blockers.

2032
01:42:48,551 --> 01:42:50,384
- That's tough.
- What a waste of talent.

2033
01:42:51,451 --> 01:42:53,783
She's listed as a libero,
but her reception efficiency is 0 percent?

2034
01:42:53,808 --> 01:42:55,327
That means zero positive passes, right?

2035
01:42:55,384 --> 01:42:58,151
She just doesn't meet the pro baseline.

2036
01:42:58,518 --> 01:43:00,683
If you've played pro for a decade
and only managed a single point...

2037
01:43:00,684 --> 01:43:02,783
that points
to a fundamental skill ceiling.

2038
01:43:02,784 --> 01:43:04,159
I have serious doubts about her.

2039
01:43:04,184 --> 01:43:07,083
She seems prone to chronic injuries.

2040
01:43:07,084 --> 01:43:09,018
Availability is a skill in itself.

2041
01:43:09,551 --> 01:43:13,718
Going undrafted twice
doesn't happen by accident.

2042
01:43:20,384 --> 01:43:21,896
I was honestly bewildered.

2043
01:43:22,584 --> 01:43:25,933
We had multiple players
who can legitimately hang with the pros.

2044
01:43:26,284 --> 01:43:28,583
Yet none of them were getting picked up.

2045
01:43:28,584 --> 01:43:34,551
I felt like far fewer names were called
than I anticipated.

2046
01:43:34,818 --> 01:43:37,918
I truly believe these players possess
pro-caliber talent.

2047
01:43:38,451 --> 01:43:41,618
Seeing those results left me stunned.

2048
01:43:42,451 --> 01:43:43,351
Next up,

2049
01:43:45,084 --> 01:43:46,418
Ha Hyo Rim.

2050
01:43:46,884 --> 01:43:50,051
(Ha Hyo Rim: setter, 172 cm,
Suwon Special City)

2051
01:43:50,818 --> 01:43:52,451
Whenever I evaluate this player,

2052
01:43:54,418 --> 01:43:57,183
her mental resilience is
what comes to mind.

2053
01:43:57,184 --> 01:43:58,351
Right, her mental game.

2054
01:43:59,118 --> 01:44:00,668
She wilted under heavy pressure.

2055
01:44:00,951 --> 01:44:03,137
She walked away from the pros, came back,
and walked away again.

2056
01:44:03,784 --> 01:44:06,361
She voluntarily terminated her contract
while serving as starting setter.

2057
01:44:06,718 --> 01:44:08,517
She stepped down to the semi-pro league,
made a pro comeback...

2058
01:44:08,518 --> 01:44:09,811
only to walk out once more.

2059
01:44:12,618 --> 01:44:14,084
First with Hi-Pass,

2060
01:44:14,984 --> 01:44:16,583
then Red Sparks...

2061
01:44:16,584 --> 01:44:18,750
Now she's suiting up
for Suwon Special City.

2062
01:44:18,751 --> 01:44:20,355
She was handed plenty of opportunities.

2063
01:44:21,918 --> 01:44:25,150
She simply couldn't handle
the psychological grind.

2064
01:44:25,151 --> 01:44:26,918
(A player who walked away
from the pros twice)

2065
01:44:28,551 --> 01:44:30,318
Even with a third opportunity,

2066
01:44:31,284 --> 01:44:33,034
I'm skeptical that anything
fundamentally changes.

2067
01:44:36,018 --> 01:44:37,872
That becomes an ingrained limitation.

2068
01:44:37,908 --> 01:44:39,901
(Franchise A hesitates.)

2069
01:44:43,484 --> 01:44:45,284
Here's my take, though.

2070
01:44:46,351 --> 01:44:50,158
A player's mental resilience can
completely transform...

2071
01:44:50,183 --> 01:44:52,518
under the right leadership.

2072
01:44:56,418 --> 01:45:00,817
If she finds a coaching staff
that empowers their setter,

2073
01:45:00,818 --> 01:45:04,718
this athlete has plenty
of untapped ceiling.

2074
01:45:05,284 --> 01:45:08,684
She's running the corporate league
with total control right now.

2075
01:45:09,284 --> 01:45:13,684
I was genuinely impressed
with how she fed the middle.

2076
01:45:14,518 --> 01:45:16,583
A setter lacking touch simply
can't make those sets.

2077
01:45:16,608 --> 01:45:17,849
Agreed.

2078
01:45:17,851 --> 01:45:19,580
That execution stood out to me.

2079
01:45:21,751 --> 01:45:24,550
As long as she keeps her composure intact,

2080
01:45:24,551 --> 01:45:28,384
she definitely has the talent
to run a pro offense.

2081
01:45:40,684 --> 01:45:42,403
There's still real hope there.

2082
01:45:44,951 --> 01:45:47,017
No matter how desperate I was,

2083
01:45:47,018 --> 01:45:48,584
things kept falling apart.

2084
01:45:50,018 --> 01:45:51,212
I reached a point...

2085
01:45:51,237 --> 01:45:53,718
where I thought about walking away
from volleyball for good.

2086
01:45:55,551 --> 01:45:59,584
I'm hoping this run with the Wonder Dogs
can help me break through those walls.

2087
01:46:01,418 --> 01:46:02,617
Of course you can rewrite that narrative.

2088
01:46:02,618 --> 01:46:04,884
With you running the floor,
I know it's possible.

2089
01:46:05,518 --> 01:46:07,218
(Look at him go.)

2090
01:46:08,584 --> 01:46:11,051
(Can an 8th pro franchise realistically
be built around this roster?)

2091
01:46:14,051 --> 01:46:15,718
With this current group,

2092
01:46:16,618 --> 01:46:20,017
building a competitive expansion team
that delivers wins...

2093
01:46:20,018 --> 01:46:20,975
right out of the gate...

2094
01:46:21,884 --> 01:46:22,844
feels nearly impossible.

2095
01:46:23,918 --> 01:46:24,979
It's just not viable,

2096
01:46:25,084 --> 01:46:26,451
not with this personnel.

2097
01:46:28,684 --> 01:46:30,717
They'd finish dead last in 8th place.

2098
01:46:30,718 --> 01:46:31,783
I agree completely.

2099
01:46:31,784 --> 01:46:33,884
- They'd lock down 8th place.
- Without question.

2100
01:46:34,151 --> 01:46:35,984
- They'd be anchored to the cellar.
- I agree.

2101
01:46:37,018 --> 01:46:37,884
Dead last.

2102
01:46:40,584 --> 01:46:44,284
Losing Pyo Seung Ju...

2103
01:46:45,284 --> 01:46:46,400
leaves a glaring hole.

2104
01:46:48,351 --> 01:46:50,917
She didn't just produce points.

2105
01:46:50,918 --> 01:46:54,551
She was the glue holding
that entire locker room together.

2106
01:46:55,284 --> 01:46:58,284
Is there anyone
who can shoulder that mantle?

2107
01:46:58,740 --> 01:47:00,284
I'd have to say no.

2108
01:47:00,818 --> 01:47:02,783
There's zero depth behind that void.

2109
01:47:05,718 --> 01:47:08,450
Replacing Pyo Seung Ju
is an impossible ask.

2110
01:47:08,451 --> 01:47:10,057
We can't replicate
what she brought, but...

2111
01:47:11,184 --> 01:47:14,884
I have more conviction heading
into Season 2 than I ever had in Season 1.

2112
01:47:16,719 --> 01:47:19,053
I'd rather work with athletes like them...

2113
01:47:19,454 --> 01:47:21,221
and help them grow.

2114
01:47:21,222 --> 01:47:25,893
I feel like they'd be
far hungrier to learn...

2115
01:47:26,008 --> 01:47:29,310
and take coaching to heart.

2116
01:47:30,446 --> 01:47:35,316
I want to show how these players
can flip an X into an O...

2117
01:47:35,684 --> 01:47:37,718
and how far they can really go.

2118
01:47:39,488 --> 01:47:41,689
Everyone across the squad...

2119
01:47:41,690 --> 01:47:44,325
needs to step up and fill that void.

2120
01:47:44,326 --> 01:47:45,494
(Everyone must step
into Seung Ju's shoes.)

2121
01:47:45,495 --> 01:47:48,863
Plus, I think it'll actually be fun...

2122
01:47:49,265 --> 01:47:52,267
to build a team from a clean slate.

2123
01:47:52,268 --> 01:47:53,301
(It could actually be fun.)

2124
01:47:53,302 --> 01:47:55,503
Now the fire's lit again.

2125
01:47:56,305 --> 01:47:57,805
I'm ready to give it everything.

2126
01:48:00,542 --> 01:48:04,011
There's a reason we made you
all watch that tape.

2127
01:48:05,047 --> 01:48:07,782
It wasn't just for a pep talk.

2128
01:48:10,286 --> 01:48:13,288
We have to show the world...

2129
01:48:15,124 --> 01:48:18,526
that we can completely shatter
their expectations.

2130
01:48:20,095 --> 01:48:21,128
Which is why...

2131
01:48:21,964 --> 01:48:24,932
we've lined up a far more brutal schedule.

2132
01:48:28,037 --> 01:48:29,771
Let's see who you're taking on.

2133
01:48:29,772 --> 01:48:30,739
(The opponents are revealed.)

2134
01:48:31,674 --> 01:48:35,810
The current club of Season One
captain Pyo Seung Ju and Lee Na Yeon,

2135
01:48:36,312 --> 01:48:37,579
the Pink Spiders.

2136
01:48:37,580 --> 01:48:38,613
(Seung Ju and Na Yeon's current club)

2137
01:48:38,614 --> 01:48:41,349
(Kim Da Sol, setter,
waived by Pink Spiders in 2026)

2138
01:48:41,917 --> 01:48:47,154
Seung Ju and Na Yeon are standing
on the other side of the net now.

2139
01:48:47,457 --> 01:48:51,459
They're active pros,
and we have to go through them.

2140
01:48:51,994 --> 01:48:55,262
Three-time V-League Championship
Finals winners,

2141
01:48:55,263 --> 01:48:56,464
Hillstate.

2142
01:48:57,733 --> 01:48:59,867
(Ji Min Kyeong, outside hitter,
waived by Hillstate in 2026)

2143
01:48:59,868 --> 01:49:02,770
Southeast Asia's premier pro club,
Lao Cai.

2144
01:49:03,373 --> 01:49:06,374
And the V-League's
newest expansion franchise,

2145
01:49:06,742 --> 01:49:07,875
SOOPers.

2146
01:49:11,146 --> 01:49:14,548
SOOPers just reconstituted their roster,

2147
01:49:15,083 --> 01:49:18,386
so they're rolling out
their full first-team lineup.

2148
01:49:22,191 --> 01:49:24,526
Counting those four powerhouses,

2149
01:49:24,860 --> 01:49:28,195
we're looking at seven fixtures in total.

2150
01:49:29,598 --> 01:49:33,034
If we drop four matches this season,

2151
01:49:33,969 --> 01:49:35,236
the Wonder Dogs will be...

2152
01:49:36,839 --> 01:49:38,006
shut down on the spot.

2153
01:49:41,577 --> 01:49:44,946
Now, let's unveil...

2154
01:49:45,580 --> 01:49:46,981
the Wonder Dogs' first challenger.

2155
01:49:52,421 --> 01:49:53,421
Wait, what?

2156
01:50:41,370 --> 01:50:42,971
Huddle up!

2157
01:50:51,280 --> 01:50:52,847
Long time no see.

2158
01:50:52,848 --> 01:50:54,749
I'm the head coach
of Shujitsu High's volleyball program,

2159
01:50:54,750 --> 01:50:56,117
Nishihata Miki.

2160
01:50:57,085 --> 01:50:59,587
(Shujitsu High School, Japan)

2161
01:50:59,855 --> 01:51:01,489
We're running it back against them?

2162
01:51:02,324 --> 01:51:05,059
Right out of the gate?
We're in deep trouble.

2163
01:51:05,553 --> 01:51:06,994
"We are in for a brutal battle."

2164
01:51:07,262 --> 01:51:09,230
That was the first thing that hit me.

2165
01:51:09,731 --> 01:51:13,000
Our toughest dogfight last season
was against Shujitsu.

2166
01:51:15,537 --> 01:51:18,139
(Last season's showdown against Shujitsu)

2167
01:51:18,707 --> 01:51:20,474
Taking the court
against the Wonder Dogs today,

2168
01:51:20,475 --> 01:51:23,544
Shujitsu High, Japan's undisputed
number-one high school squad.

2169
01:51:24,413 --> 01:51:25,580
Down the line for the kill!

2170
01:51:26,181 --> 01:51:29,350
(Led by Captain Pyo's relentless drive...)

2171
01:51:30,152 --> 01:51:31,486
Huge roof by Moon Myoung Hwa!

2172
01:51:31,487 --> 01:51:34,989
(and Wall Myoung Hwa anchoring the net)

2173
01:51:36,058 --> 01:51:39,527
(The Wonder Dogs took command,
up 2-0 in sets.)

2174
01:51:40,087 --> 01:51:42,255
(Until...)

2175
01:51:42,798 --> 01:51:45,600
(Shujitsu's suffocating floor defense)

2176
01:51:46,602 --> 01:51:51,306
(Their lethal combination plays)

2177
01:51:52,341 --> 01:51:55,610
(Shujitsu turned the tide.)

2178
01:51:55,811 --> 01:51:56,878
Enkhsoyol!

2179
01:51:57,112 --> 01:51:58,412
Where's your target?

2180
01:51:58,947 --> 01:52:00,014
Where are you putting that ball?

2181
01:52:00,015 --> 01:52:03,484
(The Wonder Dogs started unraveling.)

2182
01:52:05,020 --> 01:52:08,190
(With the Wonder Dogs running out of gas,)

2183
01:52:08,191 --> 01:52:11,826
(all the momentum swung away.)

2184
01:52:12,561 --> 01:52:15,930
I should've pulled Chae Rim earlier.
I could see her tank was empty.

2185
01:52:17,132 --> 01:52:20,734
(Coach Nishihata Miki smelled blood.)

2186
01:52:21,236 --> 01:52:26,240
(Unleashing an aggressive service run)

2187
01:52:26,808 --> 01:52:29,410
(Shujitsu brought
on their deadliest server.)

2188
01:52:30,178 --> 01:52:32,379
(Their secret weapon: Uchida Riona)

2189
01:52:33,115 --> 01:52:36,551
(Nine unanswered points conceded)

2190
01:52:36,752 --> 01:52:39,120
(The tactical substitution
that broke the Wonder Dogs)

2191
01:52:40,255 --> 01:52:41,789
(Set score,
Shujitsu High 1 : Wonder Dogs 2)

2192
01:52:41,790 --> 01:52:43,824
(Set score,
Shujitsu High 2 : Wonder Dogs 2)

2193
01:52:43,849 --> 01:52:47,352
(Set score,
Shujitsu High 3 : Wonder Dogs 2)

2194
01:52:49,831 --> 01:52:54,868
(A heartbreaking reverse-sweep defeat)

2195
01:52:55,971 --> 01:52:58,639
(Which players caught your eye?)

2196
01:52:59,107 --> 01:53:01,075
Number 19.

2197
01:53:01,076 --> 01:53:03,210
Their captain, number 19.

2198
01:53:03,211 --> 01:53:05,312
It felt like number 19 was...

2199
01:53:05,313 --> 01:53:07,815
carrying the bulk of their attack.

2200
01:53:08,684 --> 01:53:11,719
Their setter was really sharp too.

2201
01:53:13,388 --> 01:53:19,260
Number 15 stood out early on.

2202
01:53:19,285 --> 01:53:20,828
(Pyo Seung Ju, Lee Na Yeon,
Moon Myoung Hwa)

2203
01:53:21,730 --> 01:53:24,799
(Yet none of those three will be
on the court this time.)

2204
01:53:29,104 --> 01:53:31,772
Those star anchors won't be suiting up.

2205
01:53:31,840 --> 01:53:34,341
In that case,

2206
01:53:34,342 --> 01:53:36,977
we'll eat them alive.

2207
01:53:36,978 --> 01:53:38,512
Did she just say she'd eat us alive?

2208
01:53:44,052 --> 01:53:45,285
That stung.

2209
01:53:45,821 --> 01:53:49,090
I thought the rest of our lineup
held their own too.

2210
01:53:49,358 --> 01:53:52,794
(Enter...)

2211
01:53:53,428 --> 01:53:57,665
I'm Onishi Yukiji, wearing number two,
outside hitter for Shujitsu High.

2212
01:53:57,666 --> 01:53:59,466
I'm the best in the world.

2213
01:53:59,701 --> 01:54:01,602
(I'm number one in the world.)

2214
01:54:01,837 --> 01:54:03,237
Best in the world? Really?

2215
01:54:05,574 --> 01:54:07,308
(At an international youth showcase
in Italy this year,)

2216
01:54:07,609 --> 01:54:09,543
(she took the court at just 15 years old.)

2217
01:54:10,537 --> 01:54:14,240
(Capping the final
with a walk-off service ace,)

2218
01:54:14,583 --> 01:54:17,952
(she powered her team to the title
and took home tournament MVP.)

2219
01:54:17,953 --> 01:54:19,420
She took home MVP?

2220
01:54:20,922 --> 01:54:27,428
Yukiji's pure firepower, explosive pace,
and jump serve are virtually unstoppable.

2221
01:54:28,029 --> 01:54:31,498
(In this year's
regional Inter-High semifinal,)

2222
01:54:32,367 --> 01:54:37,137
(she racked up five service aces
in a single match.)

2223
01:54:39,040 --> 01:54:41,475
Her serve brings so much heat...

2224
01:54:41,476 --> 01:54:43,343
that honestly...

2225
01:54:43,344 --> 01:54:46,580
the Wonder Dogs won't even
be able to dig it.

2226
01:54:46,848 --> 01:54:50,217
I heard Kim Yeon Koung was once
crowned the best in the world.

2227
01:54:50,218 --> 01:54:52,152
Well, I'm here...

2228
01:54:52,153 --> 01:54:53,554
to take that crown from her.

2229
01:54:57,225 --> 01:54:58,726
Give me a break.

2230
01:54:59,061 --> 01:55:01,238
Staying number one in the world
isn't a walk in the park, kid.

2231
01:55:01,263 --> 01:55:02,430
(Laughs.)

2232
01:55:02,764 --> 01:55:04,398
Take it from someone
who actually lived it.

2233
01:55:06,034 --> 01:55:09,303
Since we got the better of them last year,

2234
01:55:09,304 --> 01:55:12,373
I bet Coach Yeon Koung
is dying for payback.

2235
01:55:12,808 --> 01:55:14,942
Even so,

2236
01:55:14,943 --> 01:55:16,911
we have zero intention
of dropping this match.

2237
01:55:16,912 --> 01:55:19,046
I wasn't on the roster last year,

2238
01:55:19,047 --> 01:55:20,948
but I'm starting this year,

2239
01:55:20,949 --> 01:55:22,783
so we're sweeping them 3 to 0, period.

2240
01:55:25,387 --> 01:55:28,723
We're making the trip to Korea
for this one.

2241
01:55:29,224 --> 01:55:31,926
And we'll sweep them 3 to 0
in their own gym too.

2242
01:55:45,040 --> 01:55:47,174
(Sharp tactics)

2243
01:55:47,742 --> 01:55:49,810
(Suffocating defense)

2244
01:55:50,278 --> 01:55:52,613
(Even heavier...)

2245
01:55:52,614 --> 01:55:54,682
(firepower)

2246
01:55:57,185 --> 01:56:00,387
(Japan's reigning powerhouse
makes their return.)

2247
01:56:00,655 --> 01:56:03,357
(Shujitsu High School, Japan)

2248
01:56:03,859 --> 01:56:06,861
Shujitsu is taking this.

2249
01:56:06,862 --> 01:56:09,764
Mark my words.

2250
01:56:12,968 --> 01:56:13,901
Twelve days.

2251
01:56:14,469 --> 01:56:15,636
We only have 12 days left on the clock.

2252
01:56:15,903 --> 01:56:19,807
Throwing ourselves against a juggernaut
like that on 12 days of prep is insane.

2253
01:56:20,376 --> 01:56:24,512
Still, right here on home wood,
we need to hand them...

2254
01:56:24,513 --> 01:56:25,779
a bitter taste of defeat.

2255
01:56:26,415 --> 01:56:27,715
We can't afford to lose to Shujitsu.

2256
01:56:27,716 --> 01:56:29,784
They're looking right past us.

2257
01:56:30,118 --> 01:56:31,318
We'll make sure they pay for it.

2258
01:56:31,319 --> 01:56:35,492
(Korea vs. Japan: The Rematch)

2259
01:56:35,517 --> 01:56:36,450
Onishi Yukiji.

2260
01:56:36,451 --> 01:56:38,419
(Shujitsu touches down in Korea.)

2261
01:56:42,091 --> 01:56:44,225
(Coach Kim takes a direct hit.)

2262
01:56:44,760 --> 01:56:47,228
(Shujitsu unleashing maximum firepower)

2263
01:56:47,664 --> 01:56:49,836
It brought back last year's nightmare.

2264
01:56:49,999 --> 01:56:51,900
(A free ball... Come on!)

2265
01:56:52,267 --> 01:56:54,206
(The Wonder Dogs are rattled.)

2266
01:56:55,671 --> 01:56:56,971
Isn't this our home floor?

2267
01:56:56,972 --> 01:56:58,773
Why are we the ones getting jittery?

2268
01:56:58,774 --> 01:57:00,451
They should be feeling the heat, not us!

2269
01:57:00,476 --> 01:57:02,743
Our only objective today is to win.

2270
01:57:03,012 --> 01:57:04,179
(This is our home court.)

2271
01:57:04,180 --> 01:57:05,646
(Now it's our turn to return the favor.)

2272
01:57:05,647 --> 01:57:06,881
There you go!

2273
01:57:07,116 --> 01:57:08,116
Let's go!

2274
01:57:08,251 --> 01:57:09,784
Welcome to the Wonder Dogs!

2275
01:57:10,586 --> 01:57:12,487
(Revenge a year in the making)

2276
01:57:12,488 --> 01:57:13,889
(We're taking them down.)

2277
01:57:15,524 --> 01:57:16,563
(The Wonder Coach 2)
